#. type: Plain text
#: src/config/ini-config.adoc:235
#, fuzzy
#| msgid ""
#| "Different user interface programs use different options, and not every "
#| "option is supported by every user interface. There are several "
#| "interfaces, like AXIS, GMOCCAPY, Touchy, QtVCP's QtDragon and Gscreen.  "
#| "Axis is an interface for use with normal computer and monitor, Touchy is "
#| "for use with touch screens. GMOCCAPY can be used both ways and offers "
#| "also many connections for hardware controls.  Descriptions of the "
#| "interfaces are in the Interfaces section of the User Manual."
msgid ""
"Different user interface programs use different options, and not every "
"option is supported by every user interface.  There are several interfaces, "
"like AXIS, GMOCCAPY, Touchy, QtVCP's QtDragon and Gscreen.  AXIS is an "
"interface for use with normal computer and monitor, Touchy is for use with "
"touch screens.  GMOCCAPY can be used both ways and offers also many "
"connections for hardware controls.  Descriptions of the interfaces are in "
"the Interfaces section of the User Manual."
msgstr ""
"Les différentes interfaces graphiques utilisent différentes options qui ne "
"sont pas supportées par toutes les interfaces utilisateur.  Les deux "
"principales interfaces pour LinuxCNC sont 'AXIS' et 'Touchy'.  Axis est une "
"interface pour une utilisation avec un ordinateur classique et son moniteur, "
"Touchy est à utiliser avec les ordinateurs à écran tactile.  Pour plus "
"d'informations, voire la section Interfaces du Manuel de l'utilisateur."

#. type: Plain text
#: src/config/ini-config.adoc:238
#, fuzzy
#| msgid ""
#| "'DISPLAY = axis' - The file name of the executable providing the user "
#| "interface to use. Prominent valid options are (all in lower case): "
#| "'axis', 'touchy', 'gmoccapy', 'gscreen', 'tklinuxcnc', 'qtvcp', 'qtvcp-"
#| "qtdragon' or 'qtvcp-qtplasmac'."
msgid ""
"`DISPLAY = axis` - The file name of the executable providing the user "
"interface to use.  Prominent valid options are (all in lower case): `axis`, "
"`touchy`, `gmoccapy`, `gscreen`, `tklinuxcnc`, `qtvcp`, `qtvcp qtdragon` or "
"`qtvcp qtplasmac`."
msgstr ""
"'DISPLAY = axis' - Le nom du fichier exécutable fournissant l'interface "
"utilisateur à utiliser. Les principales options valides sont (toutes en "
"minuscules) : 'axis', 'touchy', 'gmoccapy', 'gscreen', 'tklinuxcnc', "
"'qtvcp', 'qtvcp-qtdragon' ou 'qtvcp-qtplasmac'."

#. type: Plain text
#: src/config/ini-config.adoc:240
#, fuzzy
#| msgid ""
#| "'POSITION_OFFSET = RELATIVE' - The coordinate system (RELATIVE or "
#| "MACHINE)  to show on the DRO when the user interface starts. The RELATIVE "
#| "coordinate system reflects the G92 and G5x coordinate offsets currently "
#| "in effect."
msgid ""
"`POSITION_OFFSET = RELATIVE` - The coordinate system (`RELATIVE` or "
"`MACHINE`) to show on the DRO when the user interface starts.  The RELATIVE "
"coordinate system reflects the G92 and G5__x__ coordinate offsets currently "
"in effect."
msgstr ""
"'POSITION_OFFSET = RELATIVE' - Le système de coordonnées (RELATIVE ou "
"MACHINE)  à utiliser au démarrage de l'interface utilisateur. Le système de "
"coordonnées RELATIVE reflète le G92 et le décalage d'origine G5x "
"actuellement actifs."

#. type: Plain text
#: src/config/ini-config.adoc:245
#, fuzzy
#| msgid ""
#| "'POSITION_FEEDBACK = COMMANDED' - The coordinate value (COMMANDED or "
#| "ACTUAL)  to show on the DRO when the user interface starts. In Axis this "
#| "can be changed from the View menu. The COMMANDED position is the position "
#| "requested by LinuxCNC. The ACTUAL position is the feedback position of "
#| "the motors if they have feedback like most servo systems. Typically the "
#| "COMMANDED value is used."
msgid ""
"`POSITION_FEEDBACK = COMMANDED` - The coordinate value (`COMMANDED` or "
"`ACTUAL`) to show on the DRO when the user interface starts.  In AXIS this "
"can be changed from the View menu.  The COMMANDED position is the position "
"requested by LinuxCNC.  The ACTUAL position is the feedback position of the "
"motors if they have feedback like most servo systems.  Typically the "
"COMMANDED value is used."
msgstr ""
"POSITION_FEEDBACK = COMMANDED' - La valeur de la coordonnée (COMMANDÉE ou "
"RÉELLE) à afficher sur le compteur numérique au démarrage de l'interface "
"utilisateur. Dans Axis, cette valeur peut être modifiée à partir du menu "
"View. La position COMMANDÉE est la position demandée par LinuxCNC. La "
"position ACTUELLE est la position de retour des moteurs s'ils ont un retour "
"comme la plupart des systèmes servo. Généralement, la valeur COMMANDE est "
"utilisée."

#. type: Plain text
#: src/config/ini-config.adoc:249
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"`DRO_FORMAT_MM = %+08.6f` - Override the default DRO formatting in metric "
"mode (normally 3 decimal places, padded with spaces to 6 digits to the "
"left).  The example above will pad with zeros, display 6 decimal digits and "
"force display of a + sign for positive numbers.  Formatting follows Python "
"practice: https://docs.python.org/2/library/string.html#format-specification-"
"mini-language .  An error will be raised if the format can not accept a "
"floating-point value."
msgstr ""
"'DRO_FORMAT_MM = %+08.6f' - Over-ride the default DRO formatting in metric "
"mode. (normally 3 decimal places, padded with spaces to 6 digits to the "
"left)  the example above will pad with zeros, display 6 decimal digits and "
"force display of a + sign for positive numbers. Formatting follows Python "
"practice.  https://docs.python.org/2/library/string.html#format-"
"specification-mini-language an error will be raised if the format can not "
"accept a floating-point value."

#. type: Plain text
#: src/config/ini-config.adoc:253
#, fuzzy
#| msgid ""
#| "'DRO_FORMAT_IN = % 4.1f' - Override the default DRO formatting in "
#| "imperial mode (normally 4 decimal places, padded with spaces to 6 digits "
#| "to the left).  The example above will display only one decimal digit. "
#| "Formatting follows Python practice.  https://docs.python.org/2/library/"
#| "string.html#format-specification-mini-language An error will be raised if "
#| "the format can not accept a floating-point value."
msgid ""
"`DRO_FORMAT_IN = % 4.1f` - Override the default DRO formatting in imperial "
"mode (normally 4 decimal places, padded with spaces to 6 digits to the "
"left).  The example above will display only one decimal digit.  Formatting "
"follows Python practice: https://docs.python.org/2/library/"
"string.html#format-specification-mini-language .  An error will be raised if "
"the format can not accept a floating-point value."
msgstr ""
"'DRO_FORMAT_IN = % 4.1f' - Remplace le formatage par défaut du compteur "
"numérique en mode impérial (normalement 4 décimales, avec des espaces "
"jusqu'à 6 chiffres à gauche).  L'exemple ci-dessus n'affichera qu'un seul "
"chiffre décimal. Le formatage suit la pratique Python. https://"
"docs.python.org/2/library/string.html#format-specification-mini-language Une "
"erreur sera levée si le format ne peut pas accepter une valeur à virgule "
"flottante."

