#. type: Plain text
#: src/config/stepconf.adoc:63
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"'Machine Name' - Choose a name for your machine.  Use only uppercase "
"letters, lowercase letters, digits, - and _."
msgstr ""
"_Nom de la machine_ - (((Nom de la machine)))  Choisir un nom pour la "
"machine.  Utiliser uniquement des lettres majuscules, minuscules, des "
"chiffres ou \"-\" et \"_\"."

#. type: Plain text
#: src/config/stepconf.adoc:65
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"'Axis Configuration' - Choose XYZ (Mill), XYZA (4-axis mill) or XZ (Lathe)."
msgstr ""
"_Configuration des axes_ - (((Configuration des axes)))  Choisir les axes "
"correspondants à la machine: XYZ (fraiseuse 3 axes), XYZA (fraiseuse 4 axes) "
"ou XZ (tour)."

#. type: Index entry
#: src/config/stepconf.adoc:70
#, fuzzy
#| msgid "Machine units"
msgid "Machine Units"
msgstr "Unités de machine"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/config/stepconf.adoc:70
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"'Machine Units' - Choose Inch or mm. All subsequent entries will be in the "
"chosen units. Changing this also changes the default values in the Axes "
"section.  If you change this after selecting values in any of the axes "
"sections, they will be over-written by the default values of the selected "
"units."
msgstr ""
"_Unité machine_ - (((Unité machine)))  Choisir entre le pouce et le "
"millimètre. Toutes les questions suivantes (telles que la longueur des "
"courses, le pas de la vis, etc)  devront obtenir des réponses dans l'unité "
"choisie ici."

#. type: Index entry
#: src/config/stepconf.adoc:76
#, fuzzy
msgid "Driver Type"
msgstr "Exemples de configuration des pilotes"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/config/stepconf.adoc:76
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"'Driver Type' - If you have one of the stepper drivers listed in the pull "
"down box, choose it.  Otherwise, select 'Other' and find the timing values "
"in your driver's data sheet and enter them as 'nano seconds' in the 'Driver "
"Timing Settings'.  If the data sheet gives a value in microseconds, multiply "
"by 1000.  For example, enter 4.5 µs as 4500 ns."
msgstr ""
"_Caractéristiques du pilote_ - (((Caractéristiques du pilote)))  Si un des "
"pilotes énumérés dans la liste déroulante peut être utilisé, cliquer\tsur "
"son nom. Sinon, trouver les 4 valeurs de timing dans la fiche de "
"caractéristiques fournie par le fabricant du pilote et les saisir.  Si la "
"fiche donne des valeurs en microsecondes, les multiplier par 1000.  pour les "
"convertir en nanosecondes.  Par exemple, pour 4.5µs saisir 4500ns."

#. type: Plain text
#: src/config/stepconf.adoc:80
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"A list of some popular drives, along with their timing values, is on the "
"LinuxCNC.org Wiki under https://wiki.linuxcnc.org/cgi-bin/wiki.pl?"
"Stepper_Drive_Timing[Stepper Drive Timing]."
msgstr ""
"Une liste de certains des pilotes pas à pas les plus populaires, avec leurs "
"valeurs caractéristiques de timing, se trouve sur le wiki de LinuxCNC.org à "
"la page http://wiki.linuxcnc.org/cgi-bin/wiki.pl?"
"Stepper_Drive_Timing[Timming des pilotes]."

#. type: Plain text
#: src/config/stepconf.adoc:85
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Additional signal conditioning or isolation such as optocouplers and RC "
"filters on break out boards can impose timing constraints of their own, in "
"addition to those of the driver. You may find it necessary to add some time "
"to the drive requirements to allow for this."
msgstr ""
"D'éventuels traitements des signaux, une opto-isolation ou des filtres RC, "
"peuvent imposer des contraintes de temps supplémentaires aux signaux, il "
"convient de les ajouter à celles du pilote."

#. type: Plain text
#: src/config/stepconf.adoc:87
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"The LinuxCNC Configuration Selector has configs for Sherline already "
"configured."
msgstr "La Configuration LinuxCNC pour Sherline est déjà réglée."

#. type: Plain text
#: src/config/stepconf.adoc:89
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"'Step Time' - How long the step pulse is 'on' in nano seconds. If your not "
"sure about this setting a value of 20,000 will work with most drives."
msgstr ""
"_Step Time_ - Durée de la largeur de l'impulsion de pas à l'état _on_, en "
"nanosecondes."

#. type: Plain text
#: src/config/stepconf.adoc:91
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"'Step Space' - Minimum time between step pulses in nano seconds. If your not "
"sure about this setting a value of 20,000 will work with most drives."
msgstr ""
"_Valeur Space d'un pas_ - Temps entre deux impulsions de pas, en "
"nanosecondes."

#. type: Plain text
#: src/config/stepconf.adoc:94
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"'Direction Hold' - How long the direction pin is held after a change of "
"direction in nanoseconds. If your not sure about this setting a value of "
"20,000 will work with most drives."
msgstr ""
"_Direction Hold_ - Durée de maintien du signal après un changement de "
"direction, en nanosecondes. If your not sure about this setting a value of "
"20,000 will work with most drives."

#. type: Plain text
#: src/config/stepconf.adoc:97
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"'Direction Setup' - How long before a direction change after the last step "
"pulse in nanoseconds. If your not sure about this setting a value of 20,000 "
"will work with most drives."
msgstr ""
"_Réglage direction_ - Délai avant le changement de direction après la "
"dernière impulsion de pas, en nanosecondes. If your not sure about this "
"setting a value of 20,000 will work with most drives."

#. type: Plain text
#: src/config/stepconf.adoc:98
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"'One / Two Parport' - Select how many parallel port are to be configured."
msgstr ""
"'One / Two Parport' - Select how many parallel port are to be configured."

#. type: Index entry
#: src/config/stepconf.adoc:102
msgid "Base Period Maximum Jitter"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/config/stepconf.adoc:102
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"'Base Period Maximum Jitter' - Enter the result of the Latency Test here.  "
"To run a latency test press the 'Test Base Period Jitter' button. See the "
"<<sec:latency-test,Latency Test>> section for more details."
msgstr ""
"_Période de base minimale_ - (((Période de base minimale)))  En se basant "
"sur les caractéristiques du pilote et sur le résultat du test de latence, "
"Stepconf détermine automatiquement la période de base (BASE_PERIOD) la plus "
"petite utilisable et l'affiche ici."

#. type: Index entry
#: src/config/stepconf.adoc:103 src/config/stepconf.adoc:104
#: src/config/stepper-quickstart.adoc:12 src/install/latency-test.adoc:50
#: src/install/latency-test.adoc:53
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
msgid "Latency Test"
msgstr "Latency Test"

#. type: Target for macro image
#: src/config/stepconf.adoc:104
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
msgid "images/latency-test_en.png"
msgstr "images/latency-test_en.png"

#. type: Index entry
#: src/config/stepconf.adoc:109
#, fuzzy
msgid "Max Step Rate"
msgstr "Fréquence de pas maximale(((Frequence de pas maximale)))"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/config/stepconf.adoc:109
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"'Max Step Rate' -StepConf automatically calculates the Max Step Rate based "
"on the driver characteristics entered and the latency test result."
msgstr ""
"_Fréquence maxi des pas_ - (((Fréquence maximale de pas)))  Affiche la "
"valeur calculée de la fréquence maximum des pas que la machine devrait "
"atteindre avec les paramètres de cette configuration."

#. type: Index entry
#: src/config/stepconf.adoc:112
#, fuzzy
msgid "Min Base Period"
msgstr "Période de base"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/config/stepconf.adoc:112
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"'Min Base Period' - StepConf automatically determines the Min Base Period "
"based on the driver characteristics entered and latency test result."
msgstr ""
"'Min Base Period' - (((Min Base Period)))  Stepconf automatically determines "
"the Min Base Period based on the driver characteristics entered and latency "
"test result."

#. type: Plain text
#: src/config/stepconf.adoc:116
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"The important number from the result of the Latency Test is the 'max "
"jitter'. In the example above, 9075 nanoseconds (ns), or 9.075 microseconds "
"(µs), is the highest jitter.  Enter the max jitter it in the Base Period "
"Maximum Jitter box."
msgstr ""
"The important numbers are the 'max jitter'. In the example above 9075 "
"nanoseconds, or 9.075 microseconds, is the highest jitter.  Record this "
"number, and enter it in the Base Period Maximum Jitter box."

#. type: Title ==
#: src/config/stepconf.adoc:117
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
msgid "Parallel Port Setup"
msgstr "Réglage du port parallèle"

