#. type: Title ===
#: src/config/stepper.adoc:199
#, no-wrap
msgid "Adding PWM Spindle Speed Control"
msgstr "Ajouter le contrôle de vitesse broche en PWM"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/config/stepper.adoc:202 src/examples/spindle.adoc:49
msgid ""
"If your spindle can be controlled by a PWM signal, use the 'pwmgen' "
"component to create the signal:"
msgstr ""
"Si votre vitesse de broche peut être contrôlée par un signal de PWM, "
"utilisez le composant _pwmgen_ pour créer ce signal :"

#. type: delimited block -
#: src/config/stepper.adoc:212
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"loadrt pwmgen output_type=0\n"
"addf pwmgen.update servo-thread\n"
"addf pwmgen.make-pulses base-thread\n"
"net spindle-speed-cmd spindle.0.speed-out => pwmgen.0.value\n"
"net spindle-on spindle.0.on => pwmgen.0.enable\n"
"net spindle-pwm pwmgen.0.pwm => parport.0.pin-09-out\n"
"setp pwmgen.0.scale 1800 # Change to your spindle's top speed in RPM\n"
msgstr ""
"loadrt pwmgen output_type=0\n"
"addf pwmgen.update servo-thread\n"
"addf pwmgen.make-pulses base-thread\n"
"net spindle-speed-cmd spindle.0.speed-out => pwmgen.0.value\n"
"net spindle-on spindle.0.on => pwmgen.0.enable\n"
"net spindle-pwm pwmgen.0.pwm => parport.0.pin-09-out\n"
"setp pwmgen.0.scale 1800 # Change to your spindle's top speed in RPM\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/config/stepper.adoc:217
#, fuzzy
#| msgid ""
#| "This assumes that the spindle controller's response to PWM is simple: 0% "
#| "PWM gives 0 RPM, 10% PWM gives 180 RPM, etc. If there is a minimum PWM "
#| "required to get the spindle to turn, follow the example in the 'nist-"
#| "lathe' sample configuration to use a 'scale' component."
msgid ""
"This assumes that the spindle controller's response to PWM is simple: 0% PWM "
"gives 0 RPM, 10% PWM gives 180 RPM, etc.  If there is a minimum PWM required "
"to get the spindle to turn, follow the example in the 'nist-lathe' sample "
"configuration to use a 'scale' component."
msgstr ""
"Ce qui donnera le fonctionnement suivant, pour un signal PWM à : 0% donnera "
"une vitesse de 0tr/mn, 10% une vitesse de 180tr/mn, etc. Si un signal PWM "
"supérieur à 0% est requis pour que la broche commence à tourner, suivez "
"l'exemple du fichier de configuration _nist-lathe_ qui utilise un composant "
"d'échelle (_scale_)."

#. type: Title ===
#: src/config/stepper.adoc:218
#, no-wrap
msgid "Adding an enable signal"
msgstr "Ajouter un signal de validation *enable*"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/config/stepper.adoc:222
#, fuzzy
#| msgid ""
#| "Some amplifiers (drives) require an enable signal before they accept and "
#| "command movement of the motors. For this reason there are already defined "
#| "signals called 'Xen', 'Yen', 'Zen'."
msgid ""
"Some amplifiers (drives) require an enable signal before they accept and "
"command movement of the motors.  For this reason there are already defined "
"signals called 'Xen', 'Yen', 'Zen'."
msgstr ""
"Certains pilotes de moteurs requiert un signal de validation _enable_ avant "
"d'autoriser tout mouvement du moteur. Pour celà des signaux sont déjà "
"définis et appelés _Xen_, _Yen_, _Zen_."

#. type: Plain text
#: src/config/stepper.adoc:224
msgid "To connect them use the following example:"
msgstr "Pour les connecter vous pouvez utilisez l'exemple suivant :"

#. type: delimited block -
#: src/config/stepper.adoc:228
#, no-wrap
msgid "net Xen parport.0.pin-08-out\n"
msgstr "net Xen parport.0.pin-08-out\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/config/stepper.adoc:232
#, fuzzy
#| msgid ""
#| "You can either have one single pin that enables all drives; or several, "
#| "depending on the setup you have. Note, however, that usually when one "
#| "axis faults, all the other drives will be disabled as well, so having "
#| "only one enable signal / pin for all drives is a common practice."
msgid ""
"You can either have one single pin that enables all drives; or several, "
"depending on the setup you have.  Note, however, that usually when one axis "
"faults, all the other drives will be disabled as well, so having only one "
"enable signal / pin for all drives is a common practice."
msgstr ""
"Il est possible d'avoir une seule pin de validation pour l'ensemble des "
"pilotes, ou plusieurs selon la configuration que vous voulez. Notez "
"toutefois qu'habituellement quand un axe est en défaut, tous les autres sont "
"invalidés aussi de sorte que, n'avoir qu'un seul signal/pin de validation "
"pour l'ensemble est parfaitement sécurisé."

