#. type: Title ===
#: src/drivers/gs2.adoc:26 src/drivers/mitsub-vfd.adoc:37
#: src/drivers/pico-ppmc.adoc:44 src/drivers/vfs11.adoc:28 src/gui/mdro.adoc:55
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
msgid "Command Line Options"
msgstr "Options spécifiques au chargement"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/drivers/gs2.adoc:29
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"'-b' or '--bits _<n>_' (default: 8) Set number of data bits to _n_, where "
"_n_ must be from 5 to 8 inclusive."
msgstr ""
"'-b' ou '--bits <n>' (défaut 8) Fixe le nombre de bits de donnée à _<n>_, "
"dans lequel _<n>' doit être compris entre 5 et 8 inclus."

#. type: Plain text
#: src/drivers/gs2.adoc:30
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"'-d' or '--device <path>' (default: /dev/ttyS0) Set the file path to the "
"serial device node to use."
msgstr ""
"'-d' ou '--device <path>' (défaut /dev/ttyS0) Fixe le nom de la liaison "
"série à utiliser."

#. type: Plain text
#: src/drivers/gs2.adoc:33
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"'-g' or '--debug' Turn on debugging messages.  This will also set the "
"verbose flag.  Debug mode will cause all modbus messages to be printed in "
"hex on the terminal."
msgstr ""
"'-g' ou '--debug' Active les messages de débogage.  Le drapeau du mode "
"verbeux pourra être activé. Le débogage affichera tous les messages modbus "
"en hexadécimal sur terminal."

#. type: Plain text
#: src/drivers/gs2.adoc:35
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"'-n' or '--name <string>' (default: gs2_vfd) Set the name of the HAL "
"module.  The HAL comp name will be set to <string>, and all pin and "
"parameter names will begin with <string>."
msgstr ""
"'-n' ou '--name <string>' (défaut gs2_vfd) Fixe le nom du composant de HAL à "
"_<string>_, les noms de toutes ses pins et paramètres commenceront également "
"par _<string>_."

#. type: Plain text
#: src/drivers/gs2.adoc:36
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"'-p' or '--parity {even,odd,none}' (default: odd) Set serial parity to even, "
"odd, or none."
msgstr ""
"'-p' ou '--parity {even, odd, none}' (défaut odd) Fixe la parité de la "
"liaison série à parité paire, parité impaire ou sans parité."

#. type: Plain text
#: src/drivers/gs2.adoc:38
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"'-r' or '--rate _<n>_' (default: 38400) Set baud rate to _n_.  It is an "
"error if the rate is not one of the following: 110, 300, 600, 1200, 2400, "
"4800, 9600, 19200, 38400, 57600, 115200."
msgstr ""
"'-r' ou '--rate <n>' (défaut 38400) Fixe le débit de la liaisons à _<n>_.  "
"C'est une erreur si le débit n'est pas une des valeurs suivantes: 110, 300, "
"600, 1200, 2400, 4800, 9600, 19200, 38400, 57600, 115200."

#. type: Plain text
#: src/drivers/gs2.adoc:39
#, fuzzy
msgid "'-s' or '--stopbits {1,2}' (default: 1) Set serial stop bits to 1 or 2"
msgstr ""
"'-s' ou '--stopbits {1,2}' (défaut 1) Fixe le nombre de bits de stop de la "
"liaison série à 1 ou 2."

#. type: Plain text
#: src/drivers/gs2.adoc:41
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"'-t' or '--target _<n>_' (default: 1) Set MODBUS target (slave) number.  "
"This must match the device number you set on the GS2."
msgstr ""
"'-t' ou '--target <n>' (défaut 1) Fixe le nombre de cibles MODBUS "
"(esclaves).  Doit correspondre au nombre de périphériques réglé dans le GS2."

#. type: Plain text
#: src/drivers/gs2.adoc:42
#, fuzzy
msgid "'-v' or '--verbose' Turn on debug messages."
msgstr ""
"'-v' ou '--verbose' Active les messages de débogage. Noter qu'en cas "
"d'erreurs série, cela ne fera pas beaucoup de différence ce qui peut être "
"gênant."

#. type: Plain text
#: src/drivers/gs2.adoc:43
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"'-A' or '--accel-seconds' _<n>_ (default: 10.0) Seconds to accelerate the "
"spindle from 0 to max. RPM."
msgstr ""
"'-A ou --accel-seconds' <n> (default 10.0) Seconds to accelerate the spindle "
"from 0 to Max RPM."

#. type: Plain text
#: src/drivers/gs2.adoc:45
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"'-D' or '--decel-seconds' _<n>_ (default: 0.0) Seconds to decelerate the "
"spindle from max. RPM to 0.  If set to 0.0 the spindle will be allowed to "
"coast to a stop without controlled deceleration."
msgstr ""
"'-D or --decel-seconds' <n> (default 0.0) Seconds to decelerate the spindle "
"from Max RPM to 0. If set to 0.0 the spindle will be allowed to coast to a "
"stop without controlled deceleration."

#. type: Plain text
#: src/drivers/gs2.adoc:49
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"'-R' or '--braking-resistor' This argument should be used when a braking "
"resistor is installed on the GS2 VFD (see Appendix A of the GS2 manual).  It "
"disables deceleration over-voltage stall prevention (see GS2 modbus "
"Parameter 6.05), allowing the VFD to keep braking even in situations where "
"the motor is regenerating high voltage.  The regenerated voltage gets safely "
"dumped into the braking resistor."
msgstr ""
"'-R or --braking-resistor' This argument should be used when a braking "
"resistor is installed on the GS2 VFD (see Appendix A of the GS2 manual).  It "
"disables deceleration over-voltage stall prevention (see GS2 modbus "
"Parameter 6.05), allowing the VFD to keep braking even in situations where "
"the motor is regenerating high voltage. The regenerated voltage gets safely "
"dumped into the braking resistor."

