#. type: Title =
#: src/drivers/mb2hal.adoc:5
#, no-wrap
msgid "MB2HAL"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/drivers/mb2hal.adoc:17
msgid ""
"MB2HAL is a generic non-realtime HAL component to communicate with one or "
"more Modbus devices.  So far, there are two options to communicate with a "
"Modbus device:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/drivers/mb2hal.adoc:19
msgid ""
"One option is to create a HAL component as a driver see https://"
"wiki.linuxcnc.org/cgi-bin/wiki.pl?VFD_Modbus[VFD Modbus]."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/drivers/mb2hal.adoc:20
msgid ""
"Another option is to use Classic Ladder which has Modbus built in, see "
"<<cha:classicladder,ClassicLadder>>."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/drivers/mb2hal.adoc:21
msgid ""
"Now there is a third option that consists of a \"generic\" driver configured "
"by text file, this is called MB2HAL."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/drivers/mb2hal.adoc:24
msgid "Why MB2HAL? Consider using MB2HAL if:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/drivers/mb2hal.adoc:26
msgid ""
"You have to write a new driver and you don't know anything about programming."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/drivers/mb2hal.adoc:27
msgid ""
"You need to use Classic Ladder \"only\" to manage the Modbus connections."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/drivers/mb2hal.adoc:29
msgid ""
"You have to discover and configure first time the Modbus transactions.  "
"MB2HAL have debug levels to facilitate the low level protocol debug."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/drivers/mb2hal.adoc:31
msgid ""
"You have more than one device to connect. MB2HAL is very efficiently "
"managing multiple devices, transactions and links.  Currently I am "
"monitoring two axis drivers using a Rs232 port, a VFD driver using another "
"Rs232 port, and a remote I/O using TCP/IP."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/drivers/mb2hal.adoc:33
msgid ""
"You want a protocol to connect your Arduino to HAL.  Look the included "
"sample configuration file, sketch and library for Arduino Modbus."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/drivers/mb2hal.adoc:37
#, fuzzy
msgid "Create a config file from the example below"
msgstr "Crée un fichier .ini avec les valeurs par défaut"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/drivers/mb2hal.adoc:38
#, fuzzy
msgid "Set component name (optional)"
msgstr "'H' - Numéro d'outil"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/drivers/mb2hal.adoc:40
msgid "Set `HAL_MODULE_NAME=mymodule` (default `HAL_MODULE_NAME=mb2hal`)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/drivers/mb2hal.adoc:42
#, fuzzy
msgid "Load the modbus HAL non-realtime component"
msgstr "Charger les composants temps réel."

#. type: Plain text
#: src/drivers/mb2hal.adoc:43
msgid "Default component name: `loadusr -W mb2hal config=config_file.ini`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/drivers/mb2hal.adoc:44
msgid ""
"Custom component name: `loadusr -Wn mymodule mb2hal config=config_file.ini`"
msgstr ""

