#. type: Title =
#: src/drivers/servo-to-go.adoc:5
#, no-wrap
msgid "Servo To Go Driver"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/drivers/servo-to-go.adoc:18
msgid ""
"The Servo-To-Go (STG) is one of the first PC motion control cards supported "
"by LinuxCNC. It is an ISA card and it exists in different flavors (all "
"supported by this driver). The board includes up to 8 channels of quadrature "
"encoder input, 8 channels of analog input and output, 32 bits digital I/O, "
"an interval timer with interrupt and a watchdog."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/drivers/servo-to-go.adoc:25
msgid ""
"We have had reports that the opamps on the Servo To Go card do not work with "
"newer ATX power supplies that use modern switch mode DC-DC converters.  The "
"failure mode is that STG card outputs a constant voltage regardless of what "
"the driver is commanding it to do.  Older ATX power supplies with linear "
"voltage regulators do not have this problem, and work fine with the STG "
"cards."
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: src/drivers/servo-to-go.adoc:32
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"loadrt hal_stg [base=<address>] [num_chan=<nr>] [dio=\"<dio-string>\"] \\\n"
"                 [model=<model>]\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/drivers/servo-to-go.adoc:46
msgid ""
"The base address field is optional; if it's not provided the driver attempts "
"to autodetect the board. The num_chan field is used to specify the number of "
"channels available on the card, if not used the 8 axis version is assumed. "
"The digital inputs/outputs configuration is determined by a config string "
"passed to insmod when loading the module.  The format consists of a four "
"character string that sets the direction of each group of pins. Each "
"character of the direction string is either \"I\" or \"O\". The first "
"character sets the direction of port A (Port A - DIO.0-7), the next sets "
"port B (Port B - DIO.8-15), the next sets port C (Port C - DIO.16-23), and "
"the fourth sets port D (Port D - DIO.24-31). The model field can be used in "
"case the driver doesn't autodetect the right card version."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/drivers/servo-to-go.adoc:50
msgid ""
"HINT: after starting up the driver, 'dmesg' can be consulted for messages "
"relevant to the driver (e.g. autodetected version number and base address). "
"For example:"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: src/drivers/servo-to-go.adoc:54
#, no-wrap
msgid "loadrt hal_stg base=0x300 num_chan=4 dio=\"IOIO\"\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/drivers/servo-to-go.adoc:62
msgid ""
"This example installs the STG driver for a card found at the base address of "
"0x300, 4 channels of encoder feedback, DACs and ADCs, along with 32 bits of "
"I/O configured like this: the first 8 (Port A)  configured as Input, the "
"next 8 (Port B) configured as Output, the next 8 (Port C) configured as "
"Input, and the last 8 (Port D) configured as Output"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: src/drivers/servo-to-go.adoc:66
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
msgid "loadrt hal_stg\n"
msgstr "loadrt ddt\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/drivers/servo-to-go.adoc:72
msgid ""
"This example installs the driver and attempts to autodetect the board "
"address and board model, it installs 8 axes by default along with a standard "
"I/O setup: Port A & B configured as Input, Port C & D configured as Output."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/drivers/servo-to-go.adoc:76
#, fuzzy
msgid "'stg.<channel>.counts' - (s32) Tracks the counted encoder ticks."
msgstr "_encoder.<chan>.counts_ (s32, Out) -- Position en comptage du codeur."

#. type: Plain text
#: src/drivers/servo-to-go.adoc:77
#, fuzzy
msgid "'stg.<channel>.position' - (float) Outputs a converted position."
msgstr ""
"_encoder.<chan>.position_ (float, Out) - Position en unités mises à "
"l'échelle (voir _position_ échelle)."

#. type: Plain text
#: src/drivers/servo-to-go.adoc:79
msgid ""
"'stg.<channel>.dac-value' - (float) Drives the voltage for the corresponding "
"DAC."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/drivers/servo-to-go.adoc:81
msgid ""
"'stg.<channel>.adc-value' - (float) Tracks the measured voltage from the "
"corresponding ADC."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/drivers/servo-to-go.adoc:82
#, fuzzy
msgid "'stg.in-<pinnum>' - (bit) Tracks a physical input pin."
msgstr ""
"_(bit) parport.<portnum>.pin-<pinnum>-in_ -- Suit une broche d'entrée "
"physique. pin."

#. type: Plain text
#: src/drivers/servo-to-go.adoc:84
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"'stg.in-<pinnum>-not' - (bit) Tracks a physical input pin, but inverted."
msgstr ""
"_(bit) parport.<portnum>.pin-<pinnum>-in-not_ -- Suit une pin d'entrée "
"physique, mais inversée. Pour chaque pin, _<portnum>_ est le numéro du port "
"et _<pinnum>_ est le numéro de la broche physique du connecteur DB-25."

#. type: Plain text
#: src/drivers/servo-to-go.adoc:85
#, fuzzy
msgid "'stg.out-<pinnum>' - (bit) Drives a physical output pin"
msgstr ""
"_(bit) parport.<portnum>.pin-<pinnum>-out_ -- Pilote une broche de sortie "
"physique. output pin."

#. type: Plain text
#: src/drivers/servo-to-go.adoc:90
msgid ""
"For each pin, <channel> is the axis number, and <pinnum> is the logic pin "
"number of the STG if `IIOO` is defined, there are 16 input pins (in-00 .. "
"in-15) and 16 output pins (out-00 .. out-15), and they correspond to PORTs "
"ABCD (in-00 is PORTA.0, out-15 is PORTD.7)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/drivers/servo-to-go.adoc:95
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"The in-<pinnum> HAL pin is TRUE if the physical pin is high, and FALSE if "
"the physical pin is low. The in-<pinnum>-not HAL pin is inverted -- it is "
"FALSE if the physical pin is high. By connecting a signal to one or the "
"other, the user can determine the state of the input."
msgstr ""
"Une pin de HAL -in est VRAIE si la pin physique est haute et FAUSSE si la "
"pin physique est basse. Une pin de HAL -in-not est inversée, elle est FAUSSE "
"si la pin physique est haute. En connectant un signal à l'une ou à l'autre, "
"l'utilisateur peut décider de la logique de l'entrée. En mode _x_, les pins "
"1, 14, 16 et 17 sont également des pins d'entrée."

#. type: Plain text
#: src/drivers/servo-to-go.adoc:100
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"'stg.<channel>.position-scale' - (float) The number of counts / user unit "
"(to convert from counts to units)."
msgstr ""
"'(All float) ppmc.<port>.enc.<channel>.scale' - Nombre de tops codeur par "
"unité utilisateur (pour les conversions depuis le nombre d'unités)."

#. type: Plain text
#: src/drivers/servo-to-go.adoc:102
msgid ""
"'stg.<channel>.dac-offset' - (float) Sets the offset for the corresponding "
"DAC."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/drivers/servo-to-go.adoc:104
msgid ""
"'stg.<channel>.dac-gain' - (float) Sets the gain of the corresponding DAC."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/drivers/servo-to-go.adoc:106
msgid ""
"'stg.<channel>.adc-offset' - (float) Sets the offset of the corresponding "
"ADC."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/drivers/servo-to-go.adoc:108
msgid ""
"'stg.<channel>.adc-gain' - (float) Sets the gain of the corresponding ADC."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/drivers/servo-to-go.adoc:109
#, fuzzy
msgid "'stg.out-<pinnum>-invert' - (bit) Inverts an output pin."
msgstr ""
"_(bit) parport.<portnum>.pin-<pinnum>-out-invert_ -- Inverse une pin de "
"sortie."

#. type: Plain text
#: src/drivers/servo-to-go.adoc:115
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"The -invert parameter determines whether an output pin is active high or "
"active low. If -invert is FALSE, setting the HAL out- pin TRUE drives the "
"physical pin high, and FALSE drives it low. If -invert is TRUE, then setting "
"the HAL out- pin TRUE will drive the physical pin low."
msgstr ""
"Le paramètre _-invert_ détermine si une pin de sortie est active haute ou "
"active basse. Si _-invert_ est FAUX, mettre la pin HAL -out VRAIE, placera "
"la pin physique à l'état haut et mettre la pin HAL FAUSSE, placera la pin "
"physique à l'état bas. Si _-invert_ est VRAI, mettre la pin HAL -out VRAIE, "
"va mettre la pin physique à l'état bas. Si _-reset_ est VRAI, la fonction de "
"réinitialisation va passer la pin à la valeur de _-out-invert_. Ceci peut "
"être utilisé en conjonction avec _stepgen doublefreq_ pour produire un pas "
"par période."

#. type: Plain text
#: src/drivers/servo-to-go.adoc:120
msgid ""
"'stg.capture-position' - Reads the encoder counters from the axis <channel>."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/drivers/servo-to-go.adoc:121
msgid "'stg.write-dacs' - Writes the voltages to the DACs."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/drivers/servo-to-go.adoc:122
msgid "'stg.read-adcs' - Reads the voltages from the ADCs."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/drivers/servo-to-go.adoc:124
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"'stg.di-read' - Reads physical in- pins of all ports and updates all HAL in-"
"<pinnum> and in-<pinnum>-not pins."
msgstr ""
"_(funct) parport.read-all_ -- Lit les pins physiques de tous les ports et "
"met à jour les pins de HAL -in et -in-not."

#. type: Plain text
#: src/drivers/servo-to-go.adoc:126
#, fuzzy
