"It is up to the end user to supply the appropriate driver and HAL file connections according to his own machine setup."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ==
#: src/gui/qtdragon.adoc:696
#, no-wrap
msgid "Auto Raise Z Axis on Program Pause"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/qtdragon.adoc:710
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"QtDragon can be set up to automatically raise and lower the Z axis and stop the spindle, when the program is paused.\n"
"You toggle the 'SPINDLE LIFT' or 'NO LIFT' button to select the option to raise the spindle in Z when paused.\n"
"Then when you press the 'PAUSE' button the spindle will lift the amount set on the 'Settings' tab and the spindle will stop.\n"
"Pressing 'RESUME' will start the spindle and lower the spindle.\n"
"If you have the HAL pin `spindle.0.at-speed` connected to a driving pin, the spindle will not lower until the pin is true\n"
"You typically connect this to a timer or logic that detects the speed of the spindle.\n"
"If that pin is not connected to a driving pin, a dialog will pop up to warn you to wait for the spindle speed.\n"
"The spindle will lower when you close that dialog.\n"
"The amount to raise is set in the 'Settings' tab under the heading 'SPINDLE RAISE'.\n"
"This line edit box can only be directly set when not in Auto mode.\n"
"The up/down buttons can be used to adjust the raise amount at any time, including when the spindle is already raised.\n"
"The button increments are 1 inch or 5 mm (depending on the units the machine is based on)."
msgstr ""

#. type: NOTE
#: src/gui/qtdragon.adoc:717
msgid ""
"If using the Spindle lift option, HALUI can not be used to pause/resume the "
"program.  There is a pin, 'QtDragon.external-pause' available to pause/"
"resume from an external source.  You must also enable external offsets. In "
"the setting tab check 'use external offsets' If you wish to inhibit the "
"spindle when a probe tool is loaded, you will need to use an logical `or`-"
"component to combine the two spindle inhibit signals to connect to "
"`spindle.0.inhibit`."
msgstr ""

#. type: NOTE
#: src/gui/qtdragon.adoc:719
msgid ""
"This optional behaviour requires additions to the INI and the "
"QtDragon_postgui HAL file."
msgstr ""

#. type: NOTE
#: src/gui/qtdragon.adoc:721
msgid "In the INI, under the AXIS_Z heading."
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: src/gui/qtdragon.adoc:726
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"[AXIS_Z]\n"
"OFFSET_AV_RATIO  = 0.2\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/qtdragon.adoc:729
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This reserves 20% of max velocity and max acceleration for the external offsets.\n"
"This will limit max velocity of the machine by 20% +"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/qtdragon.adoc:731
#, fuzzy
msgid "In the qtdragon_postgui.hal file add:"
msgstr "The postgui.hal file"

#. type: delimited block -
#: src/gui/qtdragon.adoc:739
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"# Set up Z axis external offsets\n"
"net eoffset_clear    qtdragon.eoffset-clear          =>  axis.z.eoffset-clear\n"
"net eoffset_count    qtdragon.eoffset-spindle-count  =>  axis.z.eoffset-counts\n"
"net eoffset          qtdragon.eoffset-value          <=  axis.z.eoffset\n"
"net eoffset-state    qtdragon.eoffset-is-active      <=  motion.eoffset-active\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: src/gui/qtdragon.adoc:742
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"# Inhibit spindle when paused\n"
"net spindle-pause    qtdragon.spindle-inhibit        =>  spindle.0.inhibit\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: src/gui/qtdragon.adoc:745
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"# uncomment for dragon_hd\n"
"#net limited          qtdragon.led-limits-tripped     <= motion.eoffset-limited\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: src/gui/qtdragon.adoc:748
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
msgid ""
"setp axis.z.eoffset-enable 1\n"
"setp axis.z.eoffset-scale 1.0\n"
msgstr ""
"'axis.<letter>.eoffset-enable'\n"
"'axis.<letter>.eoffset-counts'\n"
"'axis.<letter>.eoffset-scale'\n"

#. type: Title ==
