#. type: Block title
#: src/gui/qtdragon.adoc:797
#, no-wrap
msgid "Sample postgui HAL file for combined spindle raise and Z Level compensation"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: src/gui/qtdragon.adoc:802
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"# load components\n"
"########################################################################\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: src/gui/qtdragon.adoc:805
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
msgid ""
"loadrt logic names=logic-and personality=0x102\n"
"addf logic-and servo-thread\n"
msgstr "loadrt logic names=and4,or3,nand5, personality=0x104,0x203,0x805\n"

#. type: delimited block -
#: src/gui/qtdragon.adoc:809
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"# load a summing component for adding spindle lift and Z compensation\n"
"loadrt scaled_s32_sums\n"
"addf scaled-s32-sums.0 servo-thread\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: src/gui/qtdragon.adoc:814
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"loadusr -Wn z_level_compensation z_level_compensation\n"
"# method parameter must be one of nearest(2), linear(1), cubic (0)\n"
"setp z_level_compensation.fade-height 0.0\n"
"setp z_level_compensation.method 1\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: src/gui/qtdragon.adoc:817
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"# connect signals to LinuxCNC's motion component\n"
"########################################################################\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: src/gui/qtdragon.adoc:823
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"net eoffset-clear    axis.z.eoffset-clear\n"
"net eoffset-counts   axis.z.eoffset-counts\n"
"setp axis.z.eoffset-scale .001\n"
"net eoffset-total          axis.z.eoffset\n"
"setp axis.z.eoffset-enable True\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: src/gui/qtdragon.adoc:830
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"# external offsets for spindle pause function\n"
"########################################################################\n"
"net eoffset-clear              qtdragon.eoffset-clear\n"
"net eoffset-spindle-count   <= qtdragon.eoffset-spindle-count\n"
"net spindle-pause              qtdragon.spindle-inhibit        =>  spindle.0.inhibit\n"
"net eoffset-state              qtdragon.eoffset-is-active      <=  motion.eoffset-active\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: src/gui/qtdragon.adoc:839
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"## Z level compensation\n"
"####################################################\n"
"net eoffset-clr2            z_level_compensation.clear      => logic-and.in-01\n"
"net xpos-cmd                z_level_compensation.x-pos      <= axis.x.pos-cmd\n"
"net ypos-cmd                z_level_compensation.y-pos      <= axis.y.pos-cmd\n"
"net zpos-cmd                z_level_compensation.z-pos      <= axis.z.pos-cmd\n"
"net z_compensation_on       z_level_compensation.enable-in  <= qtdragon.comp-on\n"
"net eoffset-zlevel-count    z_level_compensation.counts     => qtdragon.eoffset-zlevel-count\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: src/gui/qtdragon.adoc:845
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"# add Z level and scaled spindle raise level values together\n"
"net eoffset-spindle-count   scaled-s32-sums.0.in0\n"
"net eoffset-zlevel-count    scaled-s32-sums.0.in1\n"
"setp scaled-s32-sums.0.scale0 1000\n"
"net eoffset-counts          scaled-s32-sums.0.out-s\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/qtdragon.adoc:854
msgid ""
"The probe screen has been through basic testing but there could still be "
"some minor bugs.  When running probing routines, use extreme caution until "
"you are familiar with how everything works.  Probe routines run without "
"blocking the main GUI.  This gives the operator the opportunity to watch the "
"DROs and stop the routine at any time."
msgstr ""

#. type: NOTE
#: src/gui/qtdragon.adoc:857
msgid ""
"Probing is very unforgiving to mistakes; be sure to check settings before "
"using."
msgstr ""

#. type: NOTE
#: src/gui/qtdragon.adoc:862
msgid ""
"QtDragon has 2 methods for setting Z0.  The first is a touchplate, where a "
"metal plate of known thickness is placed on top of the workpiece, then the "
"tool is lowered until it touches the plate, triggering the probe signal.  "
"The current user system's (G5x) Z0 is set to probe height - the entered "
"plate thickness."
msgstr ""

#. type: NOTE
#: src/gui/qtdragon.adoc:865
msgid ""
"The second method uses a tool setter in a fixed position and a known height "
"above the table where the probe signal will be triggered.  In order to set "
"Z0 to the top of the workpiece, it has to know"
msgstr ""

#. type: NOTE
#: src/gui/qtdragon.adoc:867
msgid ""
"how far above the table the probe trigger point is (tool setter height) and"
msgstr ""

#. type: NOTE
#: src/gui/qtdragon.adoc:868
msgid "how far above the table the top of the workpiece is."
msgstr ""

#. type: NOTE
#: src/gui/qtdragon.adoc:870
msgid ""
"This operation has to be done every time the tool is changed as the tool "
"length is not saved."
msgstr ""

#. type: NOTE
#: src/gui/qtdragon.adoc:874
msgid ""
"For touching off with a touch probe, whether you use the touchplate "
"operation with thickness set to 0 or use a probing routine, the height from "
"table to top of workpiece parameter is not taken into account and can be "
"ignored.  It is only for the tool setter."
msgstr ""

