"commande de mouvement."

#. type: Plain text
#: src/hal/halshow.adoc:345
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"The HAL Show Area uses `halcmd` to discover what is happening in a running "
"HAL.  It gives you complete information about what it has discovered.  It "
"also updates as you issue commands from the little editor panel to modify "
"that HAL.  There are times when you want a different set of things displayed "
"without all of the information available in this area.  That is where the "
"HAL Watch Area is of value."
msgstr ""
"La zone de l'onglet _Montrer_ utilise halcmd pour découvrir ce qui se passe "
"à l'intérieur de HAL pendant son fonctionnement. Il vous donne une "
"information complète de ce qu'il découvre. Il met aussi à jour dès qu'une "
"commande est envoyée depuis le petit éditeur pour modifier ce HAL. Il arrive "
"un temps ou vous voulez autre chose d'affiché, sans la totalité des "
"informations disponibles dans cette zone. C'est la grande valeur de l'onglet "
"_WATCH_ d'offrir cela graphiquement."

#. type: Title =
#: src/hal/haltcl.adoc:5
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
msgid "HALTCL Files"
msgstr "Fichiers TCL pour HAL"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/hal/haltcl.adoc:15
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"halcmd excels in specifying components and connections but these scripts "
"offer no computational capabilities.  As a result, INI files are limited in "
"the clarity and brevity that is possible with higher level languages."
msgstr ""
"Le langage de halcmd excelle pour spécifier des composants et des connexions "
"mais il n'offre aucune possibilité de calcul.  Par conséquent, les fichiers "
"ini sont limités en clarté et n'ont pas la concision qu'ils pourraient avoir "
"avec un langage de haut niveau."

#. type: Plain text
#: src/hal/haltcl.adoc:18
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"The haltcl facility provides a means to use Tcl scripting and its features "
"for computation, looping, branching, procedures, etc. in INI files.  To use "
"this functionality, you use the Tcl language and the extension .tcl for HAL "
"files."
msgstr ""
"Haltcl fourni un moyen facile d'utiliser les scripts tcl et leurs fonctions "
"pour les calculs, les boucles, les branchements, les procédures, etc dans "
"les fichiers ini. Pour utiliser cette fonctionnalité, il est nécessaire "
"d'utiliser le langage TCL ainsi que l'extension .tcl pour les fichiers de "
"HAL."

#. type: Plain text
#: src/hal/haltcl.adoc:21
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"The .tcl extension is understood by the main script (`linuxcnc`) that "
"processes INI files.  Haltcl files are identified in the the HAL section of "
"INI files (just like HAL files)."
msgstr ""
"L'extension .tcl est comprise par le script principal (linuxcnc) qui traite "
"les fichiers ini. Les fichiers haltcl sont identifiés dans la section [HAL] "
"des fichiers ini (comme les fichiers .hal)."

#. type: delimited block -
#: src/hal/haltcl.adoc:28
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
msgid ""
"[HAL]\n"
"HALFILE = conventional_file.hal\n"
"HALFILE = tcl_based_file.tcl\n"
msgstr ""
"[HAL]\n"
"HALFILE = fichier_conventionnel.hal\n"
"HALFILE = fichier_tcl.tcl\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/hal/haltcl.adoc:31
#, fuzzy
msgid "With appropriate care, HAL and Tcl files can be intermixed."
msgstr ""
"Avec quelques précautions appropriées, les fichiers .hal et .tcl peuvent "
"être mélangés."

#. type: Title ==
#: src/hal/haltcl.adoc:32
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
msgid "Compatibility"
msgstr "Compatibilité"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/hal/haltcl.adoc:35
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"The halcmd language used in HAL files has a simple syntax that is actually a "
"subset of the more powerful general-purpose Tcl scripting language."
msgstr ""
"Le langage utilisé dans les fichiers .tcl a une syntaxe simple qui est un "
"sous-ensemble du puissant et polyvalent langage de script Tcl."

#. type: Title ==
#: src/hal/haltcl.adoc:36
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
msgid "Haltcl Commands"
msgstr "Commandes haltcl"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/hal/haltcl.adoc:40
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Haltcl files use the Tcl scripting language augmented with the specific "
"commands of the LinuxCNC hardware abstraction layer (HAL).  The HAL-specific "
"commands are:"
msgstr ""
"Les fichiers haltcl utilisent le langage de script Tcl, auquel s'ajoutent "
"les commandes spécifiques de la couche d'abstraction matériel de LinuxCNC "
"(HAL).  Les commandes spécifiques sont les suivantes:"

#. type: delimited block -
#: src/hal/haltcl.adoc:54
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
msgid ""
"addf, alias,\n"
"delf, delsig,\n"
"getp, gets\n"
"ptype,\n"
"stype,\n"
"help,\n"
"linkpp, linkps, linksp, list, loadrt, loadusr, lock,\n"
"net, newsig,\n"
"save, setp, sets, show, source, start, status, stop,\n"
"unalias, unlinkp, unload, unloadrt, unloadusr, unlock,\n"
"waitusr\n"
msgstr ""
"addf, alias,\n"
"delf, delsig,\n"
"getp, gets\n"
"ptype,\n"
"stype,\n"
"help,\n"
"linkpp, linkps, linksp, list, loadrt, loadusr, lock,\n"
"net, newsig,\n"
"save, setp, sets, show, source, start, status, stop,\n"
"unalias, unlinkp, unload, unloadrt, unloadusr, unlock,\n"
"waitusr\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/hal/haltcl.adoc:58
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Two special cases occur for the 'gets' and 'list' commands due to conflicts "
"with Tcl builtin commands.  For haltcl, these commands must be preceded with "
"the keyword 'hal':"
msgstr ""
"Il existe deux cas particuliers, les commandes 'gets' et 'list' en raison de "
"conflits avec les commandes internes de Tcl. Pour haltcl, ces commandes "
"doivent être précédées du mot clé 'hal', comme ci-dessous:"

#. type: delimited block -
#: src/hal/haltcl.adoc:64
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
msgid ""
"halcmd   haltcl\n"
"------   ------\n"
"gets     hal gets\n"
"list     hal list\n"
msgstr ""
"halcmd   haltcl\n"
"------   ------\n"
"gets     hal gets\n"
"list     hal list\n"

#. type: Title ==
#: src/hal/haltcl.adoc:66
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
msgid "Haltcl INI-file variables"
msgstr "Variables du fichier ini et haltcl"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/hal/haltcl.adoc:70
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"INI file variables are accessible by both `halcmd` and `haltcl` but with "
"differing syntax.  LinuxCNC INI files use SECTION and ITEM specifiers to "
"identify configuration items:"
msgstr ""
"Les variables du fichier ini sont accessibles par halcmd comme par haltcl "
"mais avec une syntaxe différente."

#. type: delimited block -
#: src/hal/haltcl.adoc:79
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
msgid ""
"[SECTION_A]\n"
"ITEM1 = value_1\n"
"ITEM2 = value_2\n"
"...\n"
"[SECTION_B]\n"
"...\n"
msgstr ""
"[SECTION_A]\n"
"ITEM1 = value_1\n"
"ITEM2 = value_2\n"
"...\n"
"[SECTION_B]\n"
"...\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/hal/haltcl.adoc:82
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"The INI file values are accessible by text substitution in HAL files using "
"the form:"
msgstr ""
"Les valeurs du fichier ini sont accessibles par substitution de texte dans "
"les fichiers .hal en utilisant la forme:"

#. type: delimited block -
#: src/hal/haltcl.adoc:86
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
msgid "[SECTION]ITEM\n"
msgstr "[SECTION]ITEM\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/hal/haltcl.adoc:89
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"The same INI file values are accessible in Tcl files using the form of a Tcl "
"global array variable:"
msgstr ""
"Les mêmes valeurs de fichiers ini sont accessibles dans les fichiers .tcl "
"sous la forme de tableau de variables globales."

#. type: delimited block -
#: src/hal/haltcl.adoc:93
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
msgid "$::SECTION(ITEM)\n"
msgstr "$::SECTION(ITEM)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/hal/haltcl.adoc:96
#, fuzzy
msgid "For example, an INI file item like:"
msgstr "Par exemple, un item de fichier ini comme:"

#. type: delimited block -
#: src/hal/haltcl.adoc:101
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
msgid ""
"[JOINT_0]\n"
"MAX_VELOCITY = 4\n"
msgstr ""
"[AXIS_0]\n"
"MAX_VELOCITY = 4\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/hal/haltcl.adoc:105
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
msgid ""
"is expressed as   `[JOINT_0]MAX_VELOCITY`  in HAL files for halcmd\n"
"and as            `$::JOINT_0(MAX_VELOCITY)` in Tcl files for haltcl."
msgstr ""
"est exprimé comme   [AXIS_0]MAX_VELOCITY dans les fichiers .hal pour halcmd +\n"
"et comme            $::AXIS_0(MAX_VELOCITY) dans les fichiers .tcl pour haltcl.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/hal/haltcl.adoc:107
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Because INI files can repeat the same ITEM in the same SECTION multiple "
"times, `$::SECTION(ITEM)` is actually a Tcl list of each individual value."
msgstr ""
"Because inifiles can repat the same ITEM in the same SECTION multiple times, "
"$::SECTION(ITEM) is actually a Tcl list of each individual value."

#. type: Plain text
#: src/hal/haltcl.adoc:110
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"When there is just one value and it is a simple value (all values that are "
"just letters and numbers without whitespace are in this group), then it is "
"possible to treat `$::SECTION(ITEM)` as though it is not a list."
msgstr ""
"When there is just one value and it is a simple value (all values that are "
"just letters and numbers without whitespace are in this group), then it is "
"possible to treat $::SECTION(ITEM) as though it is not a list."

#. type: Plain text
#: src/hal/haltcl.adoc:113
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"When the value could contain special characters (quote characters, curly-"
"brace characters, embedded whitespace, and other characters that have "
"special meaning in Tcl)  then it is necessary to distinguish between the "
"list of values and the initial (and possibly only) value in the list."
msgstr ""
"When the value could contain special characters--quote characters, curly-"
"brace characters, embedded whitespace, and other characters that have "
"special meaning in Tcl--it is necessary to distinguish between the list of "
"values and the initial (and possibly only) value in the list."

#. type: Plain text
#: src/hal/haltcl.adoc:115
#, fuzzy
msgid "In Tcl, this is written `[lindex $::SECTION(ITEM) 0]`."
msgstr "In Tcl, this is written `[lindex $::SECTION(ITEM) 0]`."

#. type: Plain text
#: src/hal/haltcl.adoc:117
#, fuzzy
msgid "For example: given the following INI values"
msgstr "For example: given the following ini values"

#. type: delimited block -
#: src/hal/haltcl.adoc:125
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
msgid ""
"[HOSTMOT2]\n"
"DRIVER=hm2_eth\n"
"IPADDR=\"10.10.10.10\"\n"
"BOARD=7i92\n"
"CONFIG=\"num_encoders=0 num_pwmgens=0 num_stepgens=6\"\n"
msgstr ""
"[HOSTMOT2]\n"
"DRIVER=hm2_eth\n"
"IPADDR=\"10.10.10.10\"\n"
"BOARD=7i92\n"
"CONFIG=\"num_encoders=0 num_pwmgens=0 num_stepgens=6\"\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/hal/haltcl.adoc:128
#, fuzzy
msgid "And this loadrt command:"
msgstr "And this loadrt command:"

#. type: delimited block -
#: src/hal/haltcl.adoc:132
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
msgid "loadrt $::HOSTMOT2(DRIVER) board_ip=$::HOSTMOT2(IPADDR) config=$::HOSTMOT2(CONFIG)\n"
msgstr "loadrt $::HOSTMOT2(DRIVER) board_ip=$::HOSTMOT2(IPADDR) config=$::HOSTMOT2(CONFIG)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/hal/haltcl.adoc:135
#, fuzzy
msgid "Here is the actual command that is run:"
msgstr "Here is the actual command that is run:"

#. type: delimited block -
#: src/hal/haltcl.adoc:139
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
msgid "loadrt hm2_eth board_ip={\"10.10.10.10\"} config={\"num_encoders=0 num_pwmgens=0 num_stepgens=6\"}\n"
msgstr "loadrt hm2_eth board_ip={\"10.10.10.10\"} config={\"num_encoders=0 num_pwmgens=0 num_stepgens=6\"}\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/hal/haltcl.adoc:142
#, fuzzy
msgid "This fails because loadrt does not recognize the braces."
msgstr "This fails because loadrt does not recognize the braces."

#. type: Plain text
#: src/hal/haltcl.adoc:144
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"So to get the values just as entered in the INI file, re-write the loadrt "
"line like this:"
msgstr ""
"So to get the values just as entered in the ini file, re-write the loadrt "
"line like this:"

#. type: delimited block -
#: src/hal/haltcl.adoc:148
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
msgid "loadrt $::HOSTMOT2(DRIVER) board_ip=[lindex $::HOSTMOT2(IPADDR) 0] config=[lindex $::HOSTMOT2(CONFIG) 0]\n"
msgstr "loadrt $::HOSTMOT2(DRIVER) board_ip=[lindex $::HOSTMOT2(IPADDR) 0] config=[lindex $::HOSTMOT2(CONFIG) 0]\n"

#. type: Title ==
#: src/hal/haltcl.adoc:150
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
msgid "Converting HAL files to Tcl files"
msgstr "Conversion des fichiers .hal en fichiers .tcl"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/hal/haltcl.adoc:154
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Existing HAL files can be converted to Tcl files by hand editing to adapt to "
"the differences mentioned above.  The process can be automated with scripts "
"that convert using these substitutions."
msgstr ""
"Les fichiers .hal existants peuvent être convertis manuellement en "
"fichiers .tcl en les éditant pour adapter les différences mentionnées "
"précédemment. Ce processus peut être automatisé à l'aide de scripts de "
"conversion procédant à ces substitutions:"

#. type: delimited block -
#: src/hal/haltcl.adoc:159
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
msgid ""
"[SECTION]ITEM ---> $::SECTION(ITEM)\n"
"gets          ---> hal gets\n"
"list          ---> hal list\n"
msgstr ""
"[SECTION]ITEM ---> $::SECTION(ITEM)\n"
"gets          ---> hal gets\n"
"list          ---> hal list\n"

#. type: Title ==
#: src/hal/haltcl.adoc:161
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
msgid "Haltcl Notes"
msgstr "Notes à propos de haltcl"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/hal/haltcl.adoc:164
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"In haltcl, the value argument for the 'sets' and 'setp' commands is "
"implicitly treated as an expression in the Tcl language."
msgstr ""
"Dans haltcl, la valeur de l'argument pour les commandes 'sets' et 'setp' est "
"implicitement traitée comme une expression dans le langage Tcl."

#. type: delimited block -
#: src/hal/haltcl.adoc:170
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
msgid ""
"# set gain to convert deg/sec to units/min for JOINT_0 radius\n"
"setp scale.0.gain 6.28/360.0*$::JOINT_0(radius)*60.0\n"
msgstr ""
"# set gain to convert deg/sec to units/min for AXIS_0 radius\n"
"setp scale.0.gain 6.28/360.0*$::AXIS_0(radius)*60.0\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/hal/haltcl.adoc:173
#, fuzzy
msgid "Whitespace in the bare expression is not allowed, use quotes for that:"
msgstr ""
"Les espaces blancs ne sont pas autorisés dans les expressions, utiliser des "
"guillemets doubles pour s'en affranchir:"

#. type: delimited block -
#: src/hal/haltcl.adoc:177
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
msgid "setp scale.0.gain \"6.28 / 360.0 * $::JOINT_0(radius) * 60.0\"\n"
msgstr "setp scale.0.gain \"6.28 / 360.0 * $::AXIS_0(radius) * 60.0\"\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/hal/haltcl.adoc:180
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"In other contexts, such as 'loadrt', you must explicitly use the Tcl expr "
"command ([expr {}]) for computational expressions."
msgstr ""
"Dans d'autres contextes, tels que 'loadrt', il est nécessaire d'utiliser "
"explicitement la commande Tcl expr ([expr {}]) pour des expressions de "
"calcul."

#. type: delimited block -
#: src/hal/haltcl.adoc:185
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
msgid "loadrt motion base_period=[expr {500000000/$::TRAJ(MAX_PULSE_RATE)}]\n"
msgstr "loadrt motion base_period=[expr {500000000/$::TRAJ(MAX_PULSE_RATE)}]\n"

#. type: Title ==
#: src/hal/haltcl.adoc:187
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
msgid "Haltcl Examples"
msgstr "Exemples pour haltcl"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/hal/haltcl.adoc:192
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Consider the topic of 'stepgen headroom'.  Software `stepgen` runs best with "
"an acceleration constraint that is \"a bit higher\" than the one used by the "
"motion planner.  So, when using `halcmd` files, we force INI files to have a "
"manually calculated value."
msgstr ""
"Prenons la question de la marge haute de stepgen ('stepgen headroom').  Le "
"générateur de pas logiciel stepgen fonctionne mieux avec une contrainte "
"d'accélération légèrement supérieure à celle du planificateur de mouvement.  "
