#. type: Plain text
#: src/hal/halui-examples.adoc:32
msgid ""
"To connect a remote program start button to LinuxCNC you use the "
"`halui.program.run` pin and the `halui.mode.auto` pin.  You have to ensure "
"that it is OK to run first by using the `halui.mode.is-auto` pin.  You do "
"this with an `and2` component. The following figure shows how this is done.  "
"When the Remote Run Button is pressed it is connected to both "
"`halui.mode.auto` and `and2.0.in0`.  If it is OK for auto mode the pin "
"`halui.mode.is-auto` will be on.  If both the inputs to the `and2.0` "
"component are on the `and2.0.out` will be on and this will start the program."
msgstr ""

#. type: Positional ($1) AttributeList argument for macro 'image'
#: src/hal/halui-examples.adoc:33 src/hal/halui-examples.adoc:34
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
msgid "Remote Start Example"
msgstr "Remote Start Example (Schema)"

#. type: Target for macro image
#: src/hal/halui-examples.adoc:34 src/hal/intro.adoc:252
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
msgid "images/remote-start.png"
msgstr "images/remote-start.png"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/hal/halui-examples.adoc:37
msgid "The hal commands needed to accomplish the above are:"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: src/hal/halui-examples.adoc:43
#, no-wrap
