#. type: Title ===
#: src/ladder/classic-ladder.adoc:493
#, no-wrap
msgid "COILS"
msgstr ""

#. type: NOTE
#: src/ladder/classic-ladder.adoc:496
msgid ""
"Coils represent relay coils. They are controlled by the variable letter and "
"number assigned to them."
msgstr ""

#. type: NOTE
#: src/ladder/classic-ladder.adoc:500
msgid ""
"The variable letter can be B or Q and the number can be up to a three digit "
"number, e.g., %Q3, or %B123.  Q coils control HAL out pins, e.g. if %Q15 is "
"energized then HAL pin classicladder.0.out-15 will be true.  B coils are "
"internal coils used to control program flow."
msgstr ""

#. type: NOTE
#: src/ladder/classic-ladder.adoc:502
msgid ""
"'N.O. COIL' - A relay coil: When coil is energized, then its contact that is "
"normally open (short: N.O.) will be closed (turned on, true, etc.) and the "
"current may pass."
msgstr ""

#. type: NOTE
#: src/ladder/classic-ladder.adoc:504
msgid ""
"'N.C. COIL' - A relay coil that inverses its contacts: When coil is "
"energized, then its contact that is normally closed (short: N.C.) will be "
"opened (turned off, false, etc) and the current flow is interrupted."
msgstr ""

#. type: NOTE
#: src/ladder/classic-ladder.adoc:506
msgid ""
"'SET COIL' - A relay coil with latching contacts: When coil is energized "
"then its N.O. contact will be latched closed."
msgstr ""

#. type: NOTE
#: src/ladder/classic-ladder.adoc:508
msgid ""
"'RESET COIL' - A relay coil with latching contacts: When coil is energized "
"then its N.O. contact will be latched open."
msgstr ""

#. type: NOTE
#: src/ladder/classic-ladder.adoc:511
msgid ""
"'JUMP COIL' - A 'goto' coil: When coil is energized then the ladder program "
"jumps to a rung (in the CURRENT section) - jump points are designated by a "
"rung label.  (Add rung labels in the section display, top left label box.)"
msgstr ""

#. type: NOTE
#: src/ladder/classic-ladder.adoc:513
msgid ""
"'CALL COIL' - A 'gosub' coil: When coil is energized then the program jumps "
"to a subroutine section designated by a subroutine number - subroutines are "
"designated SR0 to SR9 (designate them in the section manager)."
msgstr ""

#. type: WARNING
#: src/ladder/classic-ladder.adoc:516
msgid ""
"If you use a N.C. contact with a N.C. coil the logic will work (when the "
"coil is energized the contact will be closed) but that is really hard to "
"follow!"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ====
#: src/ladder/classic-ladder.adoc:517
#, no-wrap
msgid "JUMP COIL"
msgstr ""

#. type: WARNING
#: src/ladder/classic-ladder.adoc:520
msgid ""
"A JUMP COIL is used to 'JUMP' to another section, like a goto in BASIC "
"programming language."
msgstr ""

#. type: WARNING
#: src/ladder/classic-ladder.adoc:523
msgid ""
"If you look at the top left of the sections display window you will see a "
"small label box and a longer comment box beside it.  Now go to Editor→Modify "
"then go back to the little box, type in a name."
msgstr ""

#. type: WARNING
#: src/ladder/classic-ladder.adoc:526
msgid ""
"Go ahead and add a comment in the comment section.  This label name is the "
"name of this rung only and is used by the JUMP COIL to identify where to go."
msgstr ""

#. type: WARNING
#: src/ladder/classic-ladder.adoc:528
msgid ""
"When placing a JUMP COIL, add it in the rightmost position and change the "
"label to the rung you want to JUMP to."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ====
#: src/ladder/classic-ladder.adoc:529
#, no-wrap
msgid "CALL COIL"
msgstr ""

#. type: WARNING
#: src/ladder/classic-ladder.adoc:532
msgid ""
"A CALL COIL is used to go to a subroutine section then return, like a gosub "
"in BASIC programming language."
msgstr ""

#. type: WARNING
#: src/ladder/classic-ladder.adoc:535
msgid ""
"If you go to the sections manager window hit the add section button.  You "
"can name this section, select what language it will use (ladder or "
"sequential), and select what type (main or subroutine)."
msgstr ""

#. type: WARNING
#: src/ladder/classic-ladder.adoc:538
msgid ""
"Select a subroutine number (SR0 for example).  An empty section will be "
"displayed and you can build your subroutine."
msgstr ""

#. type: WARNING
#: src/ladder/classic-ladder.adoc:540
msgid ""
"When you've done that, go back to the section manager and click on the your "
"main section (default name prog1)."
msgstr ""

#. type: WARNING
#: src/ladder/classic-ladder.adoc:542
msgid ""
"Now you can add a CALL COIL to your program. CALL COILs are to be placed at "
"the rightmost position in the rung."
msgstr ""

#. type: WARNING
#: src/ladder/classic-ladder.adoc:544
msgid "Remember to change the label to the subroutine number you chose before."
msgstr ""

