msgid "linuxcncrsh(1)"
msgstr "linuxcncrsh"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man1/linuxcncrsh.1.adoc:6
msgid ""
"linuxcncrsh - text-mode interface for commanding LinuxCNC over the network"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man1/linuxcncrsh.1.adoc:10
msgid "*linuxcncrsh* [OPTIONS] [-- LINUXCNC_OPTIONS]"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man1/linuxcncrsh.1.adoc:17
msgid ""
"The command *linuxcncrsh* is a fully-functional text-based user interface "
"for LinuxCNC.  Instead of popping up a GUI window like AXIS(1) and Touchy(1) "
"do, it processes text-mode commands that it receives via the network.  A "
"human (or a program) can interface with *linuxcncrsh* using telnet(1), nc(1) "
"or similar programs."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man1/linuxcncrsh.1.adoc:24
msgid ""
"It cannot be stressed enough that all features of LinuxCNC are available via "
"the *linuxcncrsh* interface. It can substitute a graphical UI or be started "
"in addition to it. If your environment needs to control/monitor more than "
"one machine from a single location, this text interface may raise your "
"interest. Also, a speech to text interface may be easier to adapt to this "
"text-based interface than to a graphical one."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: src/man/man1/linuxcncrsh.1.adoc:27
#, no-wrap
msgid "*-p*,*--port* _PORT_NUMBER_"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man1/linuxcncrsh.1.adoc:29
msgid ""
"Specify the port for linuxcncrsh to listen on. Defaults to 5007 if omitted."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: src/man/man1/linuxcncrsh.1.adoc:30
#, no-wrap
msgid "*-n*,*--name* _SERVER_NAME_"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man1/linuxcncrsh.1.adoc:33
msgid ""
"Sets the server name that linuxcncrsh will use to identify itself during "
"handshaking with a new client. Defaults to EMCNETSVR if omitted."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: src/man/man1/linuxcncrsh.1.adoc:34
#, no-wrap
msgid "*-w*,*--connectpw* PASSWORD"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man1/linuxcncrsh.1.adoc:39
msgid ""
"Specify the connection password to use during handshaking with a new "
"client.  Note that the password is sent in the clear, so it can be read by "
"anyone who can read packets on the network between the server and the "
"client.  Defaults to EMC if omitted."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: src/man/man1/linuxcncrsh.1.adoc:40
#, no-wrap
msgid "*-e*,*--enablepw* _PASSWORD_"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man1/linuxcncrsh.1.adoc:45
msgid ""
"Specify the password required to enable LinuxCNC via linuxcncrsh.  Note that "
"the password is sent in the clear, so it can be read by anyone who can read "
"packets on the network between the server and the client.  Defaults to "
"EMCTOO if omitted."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: src/man/man1/linuxcncrsh.1.adoc:46
#, no-wrap
msgid "*-s*,*--sessions* _MAX_SESSIONS_"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man1/linuxcncrsh.1.adoc:52
msgid ""
"Specify the maximum number of simultaneous connections.  Defaults to -1 (no "
"limit) if not specified.  + In addition to the options listed above, "
"linuxcncrsh accepts an optional special LINUXCNC_OPTION at the end:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: src/man/man1/linuxcncrsh.1.adoc:53
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
msgid "*-ini* _LINUXCNC_INI_FILE_"
msgstr "-Wn <nom>"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man1/linuxcncrsh.1.adoc:56
msgid ""
"LinuxCNC INI file to use. The -ini option *must* be preceded by two dashes: "
"\"--\".  Defaults to 'emc.ini' if omitted."
msgstr ""

