#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man1/xhc-whb04b-6.1.adoc:6
msgid ""
"xhc-whb04b-6 - Non-realtime jog dial HAL component for the wireless XHC "
"WHB04B-6 USB device."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man1/xhc-whb04b-6.1.adoc:10
msgid "xhc-whb04b-6 [-h] | [-H] [OPTIONS]"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man1/xhc-whb04b-6.1.adoc:16
msgid ""
"The xhc-whb04b-6 HAL component supports the XHC WHB04B-6, a 6-axis wireless "
"USB pendant.  It provides a number of push-buttons, a jogwheel, two rotary "
"buttons for axis and speed / step selection and an ordinary LCD display."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man1/xhc-whb04b-6.1.adoc:19
msgid ""
"The LCD display, having a very simple firmware interface, indicates the "
"following listed information only.  No other information, such as custom "
"data, can be printed."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man1/xhc-whb04b-6.1.adoc:21
msgid "Activated axis (X, Y, Z, A, B or C)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man1/xhc-whb04b-6.1.adoc:22
msgid "Current axis position of X, Y, Z and separately of A, B, C."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man1/xhc-whb04b-6.1.adoc:23
msgid ""
"Whether machine (X, Y, Z, A, B or C) or relative (X1, Y1, Z1, A1, B1 or C1) "
"coordinates are displayed."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man1/xhc-whb04b-6.1.adoc:24
msgid ""
"Step size or velocity depending on the operating mode (MPG or Step or "
"Continuous)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man1/xhc-whb04b-6.1.adoc:25
#, fuzzy
msgid "Feedrate override"
msgstr "Correcteurs de vitesse"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man1/xhc-whb04b-6.1.adoc:26
#, fuzzy
msgid "Spindle Feedrate override"
msgstr "Correcteur de vitesse de broche"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man1/xhc-whb04b-6.1.adoc:27
msgid "Machine state such as reset."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man1/xhc-whb04b-6.1.adoc:28
msgid "Battery level"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man1/xhc-whb04b-6.1.adoc:29
msgid "Wireless signal strength"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man1/xhc-whb04b-6.1.adoc:33
msgid ""
"The pendant display, its rotary selector switch, and the component pin names "
"use designators x, y, z, a, b and c.  While this arrangement presumes a "
"machine configured as X, Y, Z, A, B an C, the pins can be assigned "
"independently as required in a HAL configuration."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: src/man/man1/xhc-whb04b-6.1.adoc:36
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
#| msgid "`--help`"
msgid "**-h**, **--help**"
msgstr "`--help`"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man1/xhc-whb04b-6.1.adoc:37
msgid "Prints the synopsis and the most commonly used commands."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: src/man/man1/xhc-whb04b-6.1.adoc:38
#, no-wrap
msgid "**-H**"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man1/xhc-whb04b-6.1.adoc:41
msgid ""
"Run xhc-whb04b-6 in HAL-mode instead of interactive mode.  When in HAL mode "
"commands from device will be exposed to HAL's shred memory.  Interactive "
"mode is useful for testing device connectivity and debugging."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: src/man/man1/xhc-whb04b-6.1.adoc:42
#, no-wrap
msgid "**-s**"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man1/xhc-whb04b-6.1.adoc:44
msgid ""
"Lead + jogwheel changes the spindle override speed.  Each tick will increase/"
"decrease the spindle override."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: src/man/man1/xhc-whb04b-6.1.adoc:45
#, no-wrap
msgid "**-f**"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man1/xhc-whb04b-6.1.adoc:47
msgid ""
"MPG + jogwheel changes the feed override.  Each tick will increment/"
"decrement the feed override."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: src/man/man1/xhc-whb04b-6.1.adoc:48
#, no-wrap
msgid "**-B**"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man1/xhc-whb04b-6.1.adoc:49
msgid "Add 5 mm and 10 mm to Step feedrate output"
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: src/man/man1/xhc-whb04b-6.1.adoc:50
#, no-wrap
msgid "**-t**"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man1/xhc-whb04b-6.1.adoc:52
msgid ""
"Wait with timeout for USB device then proceed, exit otherwise.  Without -t "
"the timeout is implicitly infinite."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: src/man/man1/xhc-whb04b-6.1.adoc:53
#, no-wrap
msgid "**-u**, **-U**"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man1/xhc-whb04b-6.1.adoc:55
msgid ""
"Show received data from device.  With -U received and transmitted data will "
"be printed. Output is prefixed with \"usb\"."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: src/man/man1/xhc-whb04b-6.1.adoc:56
#, no-wrap
msgid "**-p**"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man1/xhc-whb04b-6.1.adoc:57
msgid ""
"Show HAL pins and HAL related messages. Output is prefixed with \"hal\"."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: src/man/man1/xhc-whb04b-6.1.adoc:58
#, no-wrap
msgid "**-e**"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man1/xhc-whb04b-6.1.adoc:61
msgid ""
"Show captured events such as button pressed/released, jog dial, axis rotary "
"button, and feed rotary button event.  Output is prefixed with \"event\"."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: src/man/man1/xhc-whb04b-6.1.adoc:62
#, no-wrap
msgid "**-a**"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man1/xhc-whb04b-6.1.adoc:63
msgid "Enable all logging facilities without explicitly specifying each."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: src/man/man1/xhc-whb04b-6.1.adoc:64
#, no-wrap
msgid "**-c**"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man1/xhc-whb04b-6.1.adoc:66
msgid ""
"Enable checksum output which is necessary for debugging the checksum "
"generator function.  Do not rely on this feature since it will be removed "
"once the generator is implemented."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: src/man/man1/xhc-whb04b-6.1.adoc:67
#, no-wrap
msgid "**-n**"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man1/xhc-whb04b-6.1.adoc:69
msgid ""
"Force being silent and not printing any output except of errors.  This will "
"also inhibit messages prefixed with \"init\"."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man1/xhc-whb04b-6.1.adoc:77
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The `xhc-whb04b-6` executable needs permission for reading the pendant's USB device. There may be the need for additional udev rules. If so, this file\n"
"`/etc/udev/rules.d/99-xhc-whb04b-6.rules`\n"
"should be created with the single line\n"
"`ATTR{idProduct}==\"eb93\", ATTR{idVendor}==\"10ce\", MODE=\"0666\", OWNER=\"root\", GROUP=\"plugdev\"`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man1/xhc-whb04b-6.1.adoc:82
msgid ""
"The `xhc-whb04b-6` program can be run from the command line without LinuxCNC "
"to test a pendant.  This standalone mode is used to identify the button "
"codes produced for each button press and debug transmitted USB data."
msgstr ""

