"#endif\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man3/hal_port.3.adoc:36
msgid ""
"A HAL port pin is a HAL pin that acts as a one way byte oriented data stream "
"in real-time. An output port on any component may be connected to an input "
"port on any other component via a signal. Data written on the output pin "
"becomes accessible to the input pin. A HAL port signal may link only a "
"single writer and a single reader."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man3/hal_port.3.adoc:39
msgid ""
"A port also buffers data. Users should determine the proper buffer size "
"based upon their intended application."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: src/man/man3/hal_port.3.adoc:40
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
msgid "*hal_port_read*"
msgstr "halcmd"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man3/hal_port.3.adoc:47
msgid ""
"Reads count bytes from the port into destination buffer dest.  hal_port_read "
"will read _count_ bytes if and only if _count_ bytes are available for "
"reading and otherwise it will leave the port unaffected.  Returns true if "
"count bytes were read and false otherwise. This function should only be "
"called by the component that owns the IN PORT pin."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: src/man/man3/hal_port.3.adoc:48
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
msgid "*hal_port_peek*"
msgstr "halcmd"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man3/hal_port.3.adoc:55
msgid ""
"Behaves the same as hal_port_read, however it does not consume bytes from "
"the HAL port. Repeated calls to hal_port_peek will return the same data. "
"Returns true if count bytes were read and false otherwise. This function "
"should only be called by the component that owns the IN PORT pin."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: src/man/man3/hal_port.3.adoc:56
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
msgid "*hal_port_peek_commit*"
msgstr "halcmd"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man3/hal_port.3.adoc:64
msgid ""
"Advances the read position in the port buffer by count bytes.  A "
"hal_port_peek followed by a hal_port_peek_commit would function equivalently "
"to hal_port_read given the same count value. Returns true if count readable "
"bytes were skipped and are no longer accessible and false if no bytes wer "
"skipped. This function should only be called by the component that owns the "
"IN PORT pin."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: src/man/man3/hal_port.3.adoc:65
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
msgid "*hal_port_readable*"
msgstr "halcmd"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man3/hal_port.3.adoc:69
msgid ""
"Returns the number of bytes available for reading from port. It is safe to "
"call this function from any component."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: src/man/man3/hal_port.3.adoc:70
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
msgid "*hal_port_clear*"
msgstr "halcmd"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man3/hal_port.3.adoc:74
msgid ""
"Emptys a given port of all data. hal_port_clear should only be called by the "
"component that owns the IN PORT pin."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: src/man/man3/hal_port.3.adoc:75
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
msgid "*hal_port_write*"
msgstr "halcmd"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man3/hal_port.3.adoc:80
msgid ""
"Writes count bytes from src into the port. Returns true if count bytes were "
"written and false otherwise. This function should only be called by the "
"component that owns the OUT PORT pin."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: src/man/man3/hal_port.3.adoc:81
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
msgid "*hal_port_writable*"
msgstr "halcmd"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man3/hal_port.3.adoc:85
msgid ""
"Returns the number of bytes that can be written into the port. It is safe to "
"call this function from any component."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: src/man/man3/hal_port.3.adoc:86
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
msgid "*hal_port_buffer_size*"
msgstr "halcmd"

#. type: Plain text
