#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man3/rtapi_shmem.3.adoc:45
msgid ""
"*rtapi_shmem_new* allocates a block of shared memory. _key_ identifies the "
"memory block, and must be non-zero. All modules wishing to access the same "
"memory must use the same key. _module_id_ is the ID of the module that is "
"making the call (see rtapi_init). The block will be at least _size_ bytes, "
"and may be rounded up. Allocating many small blocks may be very wasteful. "
"When a particular block is allocated for the first time, the contents are "
"zeroed. Subsequent allocations of the same block by other modules or "
"processes will not touch the contents of the block.  Applications can use "
"those bytes to see if they need to initialize the block, or if another "
"module already did so. On success, it returns a positive integer ID, which "
"is used for all subsequent calls dealing with the block. On failure it "
"returns a negative error code."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man3/rtapi_shmem.3.adoc:48
msgid ""
"*rtapi_shmem_delete* frees the shared memory block associated with "
"_shmem_id_.  _module_id_ is the ID of the calling module. Returns a status "
"code."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man3/rtapi_shmem.3.adoc:51
msgid ""
"*rtapi_shmem_getptr* sets _*ptr_ to point to shared memory block associated "
"with _shmem_id_."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man3/rtapi_shmem.3.adoc:55
msgid ""
"*rtapi_shmem_getptr* may be called from non-realtime code, init/cleanup "
"code, or realtime tasks."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man3/rtapi_shmem.3.adoc:56
msgid ""
"*rtapi_shmem_new* and *rtapi_shmem_dete* may not be called from realtime "
"tasks."
msgstr ""

