msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man9/motion.9.adoc:23
msgid ""
"A comma-separated list of names for digital output pins.  This parameter is "
"mutually exclusive with *num_dio*, but can be combined with *names_din*.  A "
"maximum of *EMCMOT_MAX_DIO* names can be specified.  The default digital "
"output pin has names like *motion.digital-out-00* whereas **names_dout=**_is-"
"homing-x,is-homing-y_ will create the HAL pins `motion.dout-is-homing-x` and "
"`motion.dout-is-homing-y`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: src/man/man9/motion.9.adoc:24
#, no-wrap
msgid "*names_din*"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man9/motion.9.adoc:30
msgid ""
"A comma-separated list of names for digital input pins.  This parameter is "
"mutually exclusive with *num_dio*, but can be combined with *names_dout*. A "
"maximum of *EMCMOT_MAX_DIO* names can be specified. The default digital "
"input pin has names like *motion.digital-in-00* whereas **names_din=**_homed-"
"x,homed-y_ will create the HAL pins `motion.din-homed-x` and `motion.din-"
"homed-y`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: src/man/man9/motion.9.adoc:31
#, no-wrap
msgid "*num_aio*"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man9/motion.9.adoc:33
msgid ""
"Maximum number of analog IO pins is set by *EMCMOT_MAX_AIO*.  Minimum is 1, "
"if *num_aio* is not specified, it defaults to *DEFAULT_AIO*."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: src/man/man9/motion.9.adoc:34
#, no-wrap
msgid "*names_aout*"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man9/motion.9.adoc:40
msgid ""
"A comma-separated list of names for analog output pins.  This parameter is "
"mutually exclusive with *num_aio*, but can be combined with *names_ain*. A "
"maximum of *EMCMOT_MAX_AIO* names can be specified. The default analog "
"output pin has names like *motion.analog-out-00* whereas "
"**names_aout=**_feedrate1,feedrate2_ will create the HAL pins `motion.aout-"
"feedrate1` and `motion.aout-feedrate2`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: src/man/man9/motion.9.adoc:41
#, no-wrap
msgid "*names_ain*"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man9/motion.9.adoc:47
msgid ""
"A comma-separated list of names for analog input pins.  This parameter is "
"mutually exclusive with *num_aio*, but can be combined with *names_aout*. A "
"maximum of *EMCMOT_MAX_AIO* names can be specified. The default analog input "
"pin has names like *motion.analog-in-00* whereas "
"**names_ain=**_proxy1,proxy2_ will create the HAL pins `motion.ain-proxy1` "
"and `motion.ain-proxy2`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: src/man/man9/motion.9.adoc:48
#, no-wrap
msgid "*num_misc_error*"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man9/motion.9.adoc:49
msgid ""
"Maximum number of extra error inputs is set by *EMCMOT_MAX_MISC_ERRORS*."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: src/man/man9/motion.9.adoc:50
#, no-wrap
msgid "*names_misc_errors*"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man9/motion.9.adoc:55
msgid ""
"A comma-separated list of names for extra error inputs.  This parameter is "
"mutually exclusive with num_misc_error.  If using num_misc_error the "
"additional error input pins will have names like *motion.misc-error-00* "
"whereas *names_misc_errors=overtemp,undertemp* will create hal pins "
"`motion.err-overtemp` and `motion.err-undertemp`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: src/man/man9/motion.9.adoc:56
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
#| msgid "*spindles*"
msgid "*num_spindles*"
msgstr "*spindles*"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man9/motion.9.adoc:57
msgid "Maximum number of spindles is set by *EMCMOT_MAX_SPINDLES*."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man9/motion.9.adoc:60
msgid ""
"Pin names starting with \"*joint*\" or \"*axis*\" are read and updated by "
"the motion-controller function."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man9/motion.9.adoc:67
msgid ""
"By default, the base thread does not support floating point. Software "
"stepping, software encoder counting, and software pwm do not use floating "
"point.  *base_thread_fp* can be used to enable floating point in the base "
"thread (for example for brushless DC motor control)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man9/motion.9.adoc:73
msgid ""
"These pins and parameters are created by the realtime *motmod* module.  This "
"module provides a HAL interface for LinuxCNC's motion planner.  Basically "
"*motmod* takes in a list of waypoints and generates a nice blended and "
"constraint-limited stream of joint positions to be fed to the motor drives."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man9/motion.9.adoc:81
msgid ""
"The optional *num_extrajoints* parameter specifies a quantity of joints that "
"participate in homing but are not used by kinematics transformations. After "
"homing, control of an 'extra' joint is transferred to a posthome command HAL "
"pin (joint.N.posthome-cmd) and the motor feedback value is ignored. 'Extra' "
"joints must be managed by independent motion planners/controllers (typically "
"using limit3 HAL components). Extra joints maybe unhomed only when motion is "
"disabled."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man9/motion.9.adoc:87
msgid ""
"The maximum *num_extrajoints* value is equal to the *num_joints* value.  "
"(Note that using the maximum value would allow no operation in world "
"coordinates). The *num_joints* value must be equal to the sum of the number "
"of joints used for kinematics calculations plus the number of 'extra' joints."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man9/motion.9.adoc:97
msgid ""
"The *num_joints* parameter is conventionally set using the INI file setting "
"**[KINS]JOINTS=**value. The *num_extrajoints* is set by the additional "
"motmod parameter **[EMCMOT]motmod num_extrajoints=**value.  HAL pin "
"numbering for all joints is zero based [*0 ... num_joints-1*].  When "
"specified, 'extra' joints are assigned the last *num_extrajoints* in the "
"numbering sequence. For example, specifying [KINS]JOINTS=5 and "
"[EMCMOT]motmod num_extrajoints=2 for a 3 joint trivkins configuration "
"*[KINS] KINEMATICS=trivkins coordinates=xyz* uses joints 0,1,2 for the "
"kinematic joints and joints 3,4 for the 'extra' joints."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man9/motion.9.adoc:106
msgid ""
"An equal number of digital or analog IO pins will always be created. For "
"example, if *names_din* is specified with two pins, two named input and two "
"default named output pins will be created. In cases where *names_dout* is "
"specified with two pins and *names_din* with three pins, two named output "
"and one default named output pin will be created, along with three named "
"input pins. This principle applies independently to digital and analog IO "
"pins, allowing for scenarios such as having three digital pins and two "
"analog pins."
msgstr ""

