#. type: Title ===
#: src/man/man9/sserial.9.adoc:88
#, no-wrap
msgid "8I20"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man9/sserial.9.adoc:97
msgid ""
"The 8I20 is a 2.2 kW three-phase drive for brushless DC motors and AC servo "
"motors. 8I20 pins and parameters have names like "
"\"hm2__<BoardType>_._<BoardNum>_.8i20._<PortNum>_._<ChanNum>_._<Pin>_\", for "
"example \"hm2_5i23.0.8i20.1.3.current\" would set the phase current for the "
"drive connected to the fourth channel of the second sserial port of the "
"first 5I23 board. Note that the sserial ports do not necessarily correlate "
"in layout or number to the physical ports on the card."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: src/man/man9/sserial.9.adoc:100
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
msgid "angle (float in)"
msgstr "(float) _offset_"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man9/sserial.9.adoc:108
msgid ""
"The rotor angle of the motor in fractions of a full *phase* revolution.  An "
"angle of 0.5 indicates that the motor is half a turn / 180 degrees / π "
"radians from the zero position.  The zero position is taken to be the "
"position that the motor adopts under no load with a positive voltage applied "
"to the A (or U) phase and both B and C (or V and W) connected to -V or 0 V.  "
"A 6 pole motor will have 3 zero positions per physical rotation.  Note that "
"the 8I20 drive automatically adds the phase lead/lag angle, and that this "
"pin should see the raw rotor angle.  There is a HAL module (bldc) which "
"handles the complexity of differing motor and drive types."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: src/man/man9/sserial.9.adoc:108
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
msgid "current (float, in)"
msgstr "(float) _value_"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man9/sserial.9.adoc:112
msgid ""
"The phase current command to the drive.  This is scaled from -1 to +1 for "
"forwards and reverse maximum currents.  The absolute value of the current is "
"set by the max_current parameter."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
