#. type: Title ==
#: src/motion/kinematics.adoc:152
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
msgid "Non-trivial kinematics"
msgstr "Cinématiques non triviales"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/motion/kinematics.adoc:160
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"There can be quite a few types of machine setups (robots: puma, scara; "
"hexapods etc.). Each of them is set up using linear and rotary joints.  "
"These joints don't usually match with the Cartesian coordinates, therefore "
"we need a kinematics function which does the conversion (actually 2 "
"functions: forward and inverse kinematics function)."
msgstr ""
"Il peut y avoir un certain nombre de types de configurations de machine "
"(robots: puma, scara; hexapodes etc.) Chacun d'eux est mis en place en "
"utilisant des articulations linéaires et rotatives. Ces articulations ne "
"correspondent pas habituellement avec les coordonnées Cartésiennes, cela "
"nécessite une fonction cinématique qui fasse la conversion (en fait 2 "
"fonctions: fonction en avant et inverse de la cinématique)."

#. type: Plain text
#: src/motion/kinematics.adoc:164
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"To illustrate the above, we will analyze a simple kinematics called bipod (a "
"simplified version of the tripod, which is a simplified version of the "
"hexapod)."
msgstr ""
"Pour illustrer ce qui précède, nous analyserons une simple cinématique "
"appelée bipode (une version simplifiée du tripode, qui est déjà une version "
"simplifiée de l'hexapode)."

#. type: Positional ($1) AttributeList argument for macro 'image'
#: src/motion/kinematics.adoc:165 src/motion/kinematics.adoc:166
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
msgid "Bipod setup"
msgstr "Définir un bipode"

#. type: Target for macro image
#: src/motion/kinematics.adoc:166
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
msgid "images/bipod.png"
msgstr "images/bipod.png"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/motion/kinematics.adoc:172
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"The Bipod we are talking about is a device that consists of 2 motors placed "
"on a wall, from which a device is hung using some wire. The joints in this "
"case are the distances from the motors to the device (named AD and BD in the "
"figure)."
msgstr ""
"Le bipode dont nous parlons est un appareil, composé de deux moteurs placés "
"sur un mur, à cet appareil un mobile est suspendu par des fils.  Les "
"articulations dans ce cas sont les distances entre le mobile et les moteurs "
"de l'appareil (nommées AD et BD sur la figure ci-dessus)."

#. type: Plain text
#: src/motion/kinematics.adoc:177
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"The position of the motors is fixed by convention. Motor A is in (0,0), "
"which means that its X coordinate is 0, and its Y coordinate is also 0. "
"Motor B is placed in (Bx, 0), which means that its X coordinate is Bx."
msgstr ""
"La position des moteurs est fixée par convention. Le moteur A est en (0,0), "
"qui signifie que sa coordonnée X est 0 et sa coordonnée Y également 0. Le "
"moteur B est placé en (Bx, 0), se qui veut dire que sa coordonnée X est Bx."

#. type: Plain text
#: src/motion/kinematics.adoc:180
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Our tooltip will be in point D which gets defined by the distances AD and "
"BD, and by the Cartesian coordinates Dx, Dy."
msgstr ""
"Notre pointe mobile se trouvera au point D défini par les distances AD et "
"BD, et par les coordonnées Cartésiennes Dx, Dy."

#. type: Plain text
#: src/motion/kinematics.adoc:183
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"The job of the kinematics is to transform from joint lengths (AD, BD)  to "
"Cartesian coordinates (Dx, Dy) and vice-versa."
msgstr ""
"La tâche de la cinématique consistera à transformer les longueurs des "
"articulations en (AD, BD) en coordonnées Cartésiennes (Dx, Dy) et vice-versa."

#. type: Plain text
#: src/motion/kinematics.adoc:190
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"To transform from joint space into Cartesian space we will use some "
"trigonometry rules (the right triangles determined by the points (0,0), "
"(Dx,0), (Dx,Dy) and the triangle (Dx,0), (Bx,0) and (Dx,Dy))."
msgstr ""
"Pour effectuer la transformation de l'espace articulation en espace "
"Cartésien nous allons utiliser quelques règles de trigonomètrie (le triangle "
"rectangle déterminé par les points (0,0), (Dx,0), (Dx,Dy) et le triangle "
"rectangle (Dx,0), (Bx,0) et (Dx,Dy))."

#. type: Plain text
#: src/motion/kinematics.adoc:192
#, fuzzy
msgid "We can easily see that:"
msgstr ""
"Nous pouvons voir aisément que *AD^2^=x^2^+y^2^*, de même que *BD^2^=(Bx-"
"x)^2^+y^2^*."

#. type: Target for macro image
#: src/motion/kinematics.adoc:193
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
msgid "images/kinematics-math-01.png"
msgstr "images/kinematics-math-01.png"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/motion/kinematics.adoc:196
#, fuzzy
msgid "likewise:"
msgstr "likewise:"

#. type: Target for macro image
#: src/motion/kinematics.adoc:197
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
msgid "images/kinematics-math-02.png"
msgstr "images/kinematics-math-02.png"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/motion/kinematics.adoc:200
#, fuzzy
msgid "If we subtract one from the other we will get:"
msgstr ""
"Si nous soustrayons l'un de l'autre nous aurons: *AD^2^-BD^2^=x^2^+y^2^-"
"x^2^+2*x*Bx-Bx^2^-y^2^*"

#. type: Target for macro image
#: src/motion/kinematics.adoc:201
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
msgid "images/kinematics-math-03.png"
msgstr "images/kinematics-math-03.png"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/motion/kinematics.adoc:204
#, fuzzy
msgid "and therefore:"
msgstr "et par conséquent: *x=(AD^2^-BD^2^+Bx^2^)/(2*Bx)*"

#. type: Target for macro image
#: src/motion/kinematics.adoc:205
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
msgid "images/kinematics-math-04.png"
msgstr "images/kinematics-math-04.png"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/motion/kinematics.adoc:208
#, fuzzy
msgid "From there we calculate:"
msgstr "De là nous calculons: *y=sqrt(AD^2^-x^2^)*"

#. type: Target for macro image
#: src/motion/kinematics.adoc:209
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
msgid "images/kinematics-math-05.png"
msgstr "images/kinematics-math-05.png"

#. we can easily see that latexmath:[$AD^{2}=x^{2}+y^{2}$], likewise
#. latexmath:[$BD^{2}=(Bx-x)^{2}+y^{2}$].
#. If we subtract one from the other we will get:
#. latexmath::[\[AD^{2}-BD^{2}=x^{2}+y^{2}-x^{2}+2*x*Bx-Bx^{2}-y^{2}\]]
#. and therefore:
#. latexmath::[\[x=\frac{AD^{2}-BD^{2}+Bx^{2}}{2*Bx}\]]
#. From there we calculate:
#. latexmath::[\[y=\sqrt{AD^{2}-x^{2}}\]]
#. type: Plain text
#: src/motion/kinematics.adoc:233
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Note that the calculation for y involves the square root of a difference, "
"which may not result in a real number. If there is no single Cartesian "
"coordinate for this joint position, then the position is said to be a "
"singularity. In this case, the forward kinematics return -1."
msgstr ""
"Noter que le calcul inclus la racine carrée de la différence, mais qu'il "
"n'en résulte pas un nombre réel. Si il n'y a aucune coordonnée Cartésienne "
"pour la position de cette articulation, alors la position est dite "
"singulière. Dans ce cas, la cinématique inverse retourne -1."

#. type: Plain text
#: src/motion/kinematics.adoc:235
#, fuzzy
msgid "Translated to actual code:"
msgstr "Traduction en code:"

#. type: delimited block -
#: src/motion/kinematics.adoc:245
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
msgid ""
"double AD2 = joints[0] * joints[0];\n"
"double BD2 = joints[1] * joints[1];\n"
"double x = (AD2 - BD2 + Bx * Bx) / (2 * Bx);\n"
"double y2 = AD2 - x * x;\n"
"if(y2 < 0) return -1;\n"
"pos->tran.x = x;\n"
"pos->tran.y = sqrt(y2);\n"
"return 0;\n"
msgstr ""
"double AD2 = joints[0] * joints[0];\n"
"double BD2 = joints[1] * joints[1];\n"
"double x = (AD2 - BD2 + Bx * Bx) / (2 * Bx);\n"
"double y2 = AD2 - x * x;\n"
"if(y2 < 0) return -1;\n"
"pos->tran.x = x;\n"
"pos->tran.y = sqrt(y2);\n"
"return 0;\n"

#. type: Title ===
#: src/motion/kinematics.adoc:247
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
msgid "Inverse transformation"
msgstr "Transformation inverse"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/motion/kinematics.adoc:251
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"The inverse kinematics is much easier in our example, as we can write it "
"directly:"
msgstr ""
"La cinématique inverse est beaucoup plus simple dans notre exemple, de sorte "
"que nous pouvons l'écrire directement:"

#. type: Target for macro image
#: src/motion/kinematics.adoc:252
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
msgid "images/kinematics-math-06.png"
msgstr "images/kinematics-math-06.png"

#. type: Target for macro image
#: src/motion/kinematics.adoc:254
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
msgid "images/kinematics-math-07.png"
msgstr "images/kinematics-math-07.png"

#. latexmath::[\[AD=\sqrt{x^{2}+y^{2}}\]]
#. latexmath::[\[BD=\sqrt{(Bx-x)^{2}+y^{2}}\]]
#. type: Plain text
#: src/motion/kinematics.adoc:263
#, fuzzy
msgid "or translated to actual code:"
msgstr "ou traduite en code:"

#. type: delimited block -
#: src/motion/kinematics.adoc:270
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
msgid ""
"double x2 = pos->tran.x * pos->tran.x;\n"
"double y2 = pos->tran.y * pos->tran.y;\n"
"joints[0] = sqrt(x2 + y2);\n"
"joints[1] = sqrt((Bx - pos->tran.x)*(Bx - pos->tran.x) + y2);\n"
"return 0;\n"
msgstr ""
"double x2 = pos->tran.x * pos->tran.x;\n"
"double y2 = pos->tran.y * pos->tran.y;\n"
"joints[0] = sqrt(x2 + y2);\n"
"joints[1] = sqrt((Bx - pos->tran.x)*(Bx - pos->tran.x) + y2);\n"
"return 0;\n"

