#: src/plasma/qtplasmac.adoc:3293
msgid "To run G-code, just enter the code to be run."
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: src/plasma/qtplasmac.adoc:3297
#, no-wrap
msgid "n Code = G0 X100\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/plasma/qtplasmac.adoc:3300
#, fuzzy
msgid "To run an existing subroutine."
msgstr "Création d'un sous-programme"

#. type: delimited block -
#: src/plasma/qtplasmac.adoc:3304
#, no-wrap
msgid "n Code = o<the_subroutine> call\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/plasma/qtplasmac.adoc:3308
msgid ""
"_<machine_name>_.ini file variables can be entered by using the standard "
"LinuxCNC G-code format.  If expressions are included, then they need to be "
"surrounded by brackets."
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: src/plasma/qtplasmac.adoc:3313
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"n Code = G0 X#<_ini[joint_0]home> Y1\n"
"n Code = G53 G0 Z[#<_ini[axis_z]max_limit> - 1.001]\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/plasma/qtplasmac.adoc:3318
msgid ""
"_<machine_name>_.prefs file variables and also _<machine_name>_.ini "
"variables can be entered by enclosing each option in *{}* .  You must put a "
"space after each *}* if there are any following characters.  If expressions "
"are included, then they need to be surrounded by brackets."
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: src/plasma/qtplasmac.adoc:3324
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"BUTTON_n_CODE = G0 X{LASER_OFFSET X axis} Y{LASER_OFFSET Y axis}\n"
"BUTTON_n_CODE = G0 X{JOINT_0 HOME} Y1\n"
"BUTTON_n_CODE = G53 G0 Z[{AXIS_Z MAX_LIMIT} - 1.001]\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/plasma/qtplasmac.adoc:3328
msgid ""
"Multiple codes can be run by separating the codes with a \"\\\" (backslash) "
"character.  The exception is the special commands which are required to be a "
"single command per button."
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: src/plasma/qtplasmac.adoc:3332
#, no-wrap
msgid "n Code = G0 X0 Y0 \\ G1 X5 \\ G1 Y5\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/plasma/qtplasmac.adoc:3335
msgid "External commands and G-code may be mixed on the same button."
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: src/plasma/qtplasmac.adoc:3339
#, no-wrap
msgid "n Code = %halshow \\ g0x.5y.5 \\ %halmeter\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Block title
#: src/plasma/qtplasmac.adoc:3342
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
#| msgid "*Manual mode*"
msgid "*Dual Code*"
msgstr "*Mode manuel*"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/plasma/qtplasmac.adoc:3346
msgid ""
"Dual Code allows the running of two code snippets alternately with each "
"button press.  The button text will alternate with each button press and the "
"indicator light may be optionally enabled."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/plasma/qtplasmac.adoc:3348
msgid ""
"It is mandatory to specify the button code in the following order: \"dual-"
"code\", the first code, the alternate button text, and the second code "
"separated by double semicolons."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: src/plasma/qtplasmac.adoc:3348
#, no-wrap
msgid "If an indicator is required then optionally add \""
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/plasma/qtplasmac.adoc:3349
msgid "true\" at the end."
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: src/plasma/qtplasmac.adoc:3353
#, no-wrap
msgid "n Code = dual-code ;; code1 ;; name1 ;; code2 ;; true\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/plasma/qtplasmac.adoc:3356
msgid ""
"On the first button press, code1 will be run, the button text will change to "
"name1, and if \"true\" is specified the indicator will light."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/plasma/qtplasmac.adoc:3358
msgid ""
"On the second button press, code2 will be run, the button text will change "
"to n Name, and the indicator will extinguish if lit."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/plasma/qtplasmac.adoc:3360
msgid ""
"code1 and code2 both follow the rule of the preceding code explanations, "
"<<plasma:button-cmds,External commands>>, <<plasma:button-py,Python code>>, "
"and <<plasma:button-code,G-code>>. Multiple codes as well as mixing codes "
"are allowed."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/plasma/qtplasmac.adoc:3362
msgid ""
"The following code will allow the user to use a single button to run two "
"code snippets alternately each button press:"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: src/plasma/qtplasmac.adoc:3367
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"n Name = X+10\n"
"n Code = dual-code ;; G91\\G0X10\\G90 ;; X-10 ;; G91\\G0X-10\\G90\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/plasma/qtplasmac.adoc:3371
msgid ""
"The original label will be X+10, when pressed the torch will move positive "
"10 in the X axis and the label will change to X-10.  When pressed again the "
"torch will move negative 10 in the X axis and the label will change to X+10."
msgstr ""

#. type: Block title
#: src/plasma/qtplasmac.adoc:3372
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
#| msgid "Terminal Commands"
msgid "Special Commands"
msgstr "Commandes du terminal"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/plasma/qtplasmac.adoc:3375
msgid ""
"The following commands must be a single command per user button, and the "
"button code must start with the special command. The exception is "
"<<plasma:button-laser,toggle-laser>> which may be appear anywhere in the "
"code as demonstrated below."
msgstr ""

#. type: Block title
#: src/plasma/qtplasmac.adoc:3377
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
msgid "*Toggle HAL Pin*"
msgstr "Broches de HAL"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/plasma/qtplasmac.adoc:3380
msgid ""
"The following code will allow the user to use a button to invert the current "
"state of a HAL bit pin:"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: src/plasma/qtplasmac.adoc:3384
#, no-wrap
msgid "n Code = toggle-halpin the-hal-pin-name\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/plasma/qtplasmac.adoc:3387 src/plasma/qtplasmac.adoc:3450
msgid ""
"This code is required to be used as a single command and may only control "
"one HAL bit pin per button."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/plasma/qtplasmac.adoc:3389 src/plasma/qtplasmac.adoc:3454
msgid "The button colors will follow the state of the HAL pin."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/plasma/qtplasmac.adoc:3392
msgid ""
"After setting the code, upon clicking, the button will invert colors, and "
"the HAL pin will invert pin state.  The button will stay \"latched\" until "
"the button is clicked again, which will return the button to the original "
"colors and the HAL pin to the original pin state."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/plasma/qtplasmac.adoc:3395
msgid ""
"It is also possible for the user to specify alternate text which will "
"display on the button while ever it is in the latched-on condition.  To "
"specify the alternate text, use a double semicolon followed by the required "
"text. This must be the last item in the button code."
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: src/plasma/qtplasmac.adoc:3399
#, no-wrap
msgid "n Code = toggle-halpin the-hal-pin-name ;; PIN\\TOGGLED\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/plasma/qtplasmac.adoc:3404
msgid ""
"There are three <<plasma:ext-hal-pin,External HAL Pins>> that are available "
"to toggle as an output, the pin names are `qtplasmac.ext_out_0`, "
"`qtplasmac.ext_out_1`, and `qtplasmac.ext_out_2`.  HAL connections to these "
"HAL pins need to be specified in a postgui HAL file as the HAL pins are not "
"available until the QtPlasmaC GUI has loaded."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/plasma/qtplasmac.adoc:3406
msgid ""
"For toggle-halpin buttons, it is possible for the user to mark the "
"associated HAL pin as being required to be turned \"ON\" before starting a "
"cut sequence by adding \"cutcritical\" after the HAL pin in the button code. "
"If *TORCH ENABLE* is checked and *CYCLE START*, *MANUAL CUT*, or *SINGLE "
"CUT* are initiated while the \"cutcritical\" button is not \"ON\" then the "
"user will receive a dialog warning them as such and asking to CONTINUE or "
"CANCEL. The dialog will list all untoggled buttons with a corresponding "
"checkbox and allow the user to choose which of the buttons should be toggled "
"automatically upon clicking CONTINUE."
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: src/plasma/qtplasmac.adoc:3410
#, no-wrap
msgid "n Code = toggle-halpin the-hal-pin-name cutcritical\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Block title
#: src/plasma/qtplasmac.adoc:3413
#, no-wrap
msgid "*Toggle Alignment Laser HAL Pin*"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/plasma/qtplasmac.adoc:3416
msgid ""
"The following code will allow the user to use a button to invert the current "
"state of the alignment laser HAL bit pin:"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: src/plasma/qtplasmac.adoc:3420
#, no-wrap
msgid "n Code = toggle-laser\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/plasma/qtplasmac.adoc:3423
msgid ""
"This code is also able to be used as a multiple command with G-code or "
"external commands but may control only the alignment laser HAL bit pin."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/plasma/qtplasmac.adoc:3425
msgid "The button colors will follow the state of the alignment laser HAL pin."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/plasma/qtplasmac.adoc:3429
msgid ""
"After setting the code, upon clicking, the button will invert colors, and "
"the alignment laser HAL pin will invert pin state.  The button will stay "
"\"latched\" until the button is clicked again, which will return the button "
"to the original colors and the alignment laser HAL pin to the original pin "
"state."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/plasma/qtplasmac.adoc:3431
msgid ""
"The following code would allow the user to use a button to invert the "
"current state of the alignment laser HAL bit pin and then move the X and Y "
"axes to the offset for the alignment laser as specified in the "
"_<machine_name>_.prefs file:"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: src/plasma/qtplasmac.adoc:3435
#, no-wrap
msgid "n Code = G0 X{LASER_OFFSET X axis} Y{LASER_OFFSET Y axis} \\ toggle-laser\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/plasma/qtplasmac.adoc:3438
msgid ""
"The position of the \"toggle-laser\" command is not important as it is "
"always the first command actioned regardless of position."
msgstr ""

#. type: Block title
#: src/plasma/qtplasmac.adoc:3440
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
msgid "Pulse HAL Pin"
msgstr "Broches de HAL"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/plasma/qtplasmac.adoc:3443
msgid ""
"The following code will allow the user to use a button to pulse a HAL bit "
"pin for a duration of 0.5 seconds:"
