msgid "Debugging Embedded Python code"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/remap/remap.adoc:1730
msgid ""
"Debugging of embedded Python code is harder than debugging normal Python "
"scripts, and only a limited supply of debuggers exists.  A working open-"
"source based solution is to use the https://www.eclipse.org[Eclipse IDE], "
"and the https://www.pydev.org[PydDev] Eclipse plug in and its https://"
"pydev.org/manual_adv_remote_debugger.html[remote debugging feature]."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/remap/remap.adoc:1732
msgid "To use this approach:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/remap/remap.adoc:1734
msgid ""
"Install Eclipse via the the 'Ubuntu Software Center' (choose first "
"selection)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/remap/remap.adoc:1735
msgid ""
"Install the PyDev plug in from the https://pydev.org/updates[Pydev Update "
"Site]."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/remap/remap.adoc:1736
msgid "Setup the LinuxCNC source tree as an Eclipse project."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/remap/remap.adoc:1737
msgid "Start the Pydev Debug Server in Eclipse."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/remap/remap.adoc:1740
msgid ""
"Make sure the embedded Python code can find the `pydevd.py` module which "
"comes with that plug in - it is buried somewhere deep under the Eclipse "
"install directory.  Set the the `pydevd` variable in `util.py` to reflect "
"this directory location."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/remap/remap.adoc:1741
msgid ""
"Add `import pydevd` to your Python module - see example `util.py` and "
"`remap.py`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/remap/remap.adoc:1743
msgid ""
"Call `pydevd.settrace()` in your module at some point to connect to the "
"Eclipse Python debug server - here you can set breakpoints in your code, "
"inspect variables, step etc. as usual."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/remap/remap.adoc:1745
msgid ""
"`pydevd.settrace()` will block execution if Eclipse and the Pydev debug "
"server have not been started."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/remap/remap.adoc:1748
msgid ""
"To cover the last two steps: the `o<pydevd>` procedure helps to get into the "
"debugger from MDI mode.  See also the `call_pydevd` function in `util.py` "
"and its usage in `remap.involute` to set a breakpoint."
