#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/eoffset_per_angle.9:38
msgid ""
"An offset is computed (from one of several functions) based on an input "
"angle in degrees\\&. The angle could be a rotary coordinate value or a "
"spindle angle\\&."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/eoffset_per_angle.9:40
msgid ""
"The computed offset is represented as an s32 B<kcounts> output pin that is a "
"compatible input to external offset pins like B<axis\\&.L\\&.eoffset-counts> "
"where B<L> is the coordinate letter\\&. Scaling of the s32 B<kcounts> is "
"controlled by the input (B<k>) \\(em its reciprocal value is presented on an "
"output pin B<kreciprocal> for connection to B<axis\\&.L\\&.eoffset-"
"scale>\\&. The default value for B<k> should be suitable for most uses\\&."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/eoffset_per_angle.9:42
msgid ""
"The built-in functions use pins B<fmult> and B<rfraction> to control the "
"output frequency (or number of polygon sides) and amplitude respectively\\&. "
"The B<rfraction> pin controls the offset amplitude as a fraction of the "
"B<radius-ref> pin\\&."
msgstr ""

